#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Working Space"
msgstr "Radni prostor"

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So I told &digikam; where to find my monitor profile and I have a camera "
"profile that I applied to the image file produced by my raw processing "
"software. What's the next step in color management?"
msgstr ""
"Dakle rekli smo &digikam;u gdje da pronađe profil  našeg monitora i imamo "
"profil kamere koji smo primjenili na sliku koju je proizveo softver za "
"obradu raw-a. Koji je sljedeći korak u upravjanju bojama?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to choose a working color space so you can edit your image. LCMS "
"will transform your image from your camera color space to your chosen "
"working space, via the PCS specified by your camera color profile."
msgstr ""
"Morate izabrati radni prostor boja da možete uređivati slike. LCMS će "
"transformisati sliku iza radnog prostora kamere u izabrani radni prostor, "
"preko PCS-a specificiraanog preko profila kamere."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why cannot I just edit my images in the color space described by the camera "
"profile?"
msgstr ""
"Zašto jednostavno ne mogu urediti slike u prostoru koji opisuje moj profil "
"kamere?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After all, the camera profile should provide the best \"fit\" to the colors "
"recorded by my camera, as processed by my raw processing procedure, right? "
"Wikipedia says, \"Working spaces, such as sRGB or Adobe RGB, are color "
"spaces that facilitate good results while editing. For instance, pixels with "
"equal values of RGB should appear neutral.\" \"[P]ixels with equal values of "
"RGB should appear neutral\" just means that for any given pixel in an image "
"that has been converted to a suitable working space, if R=G=B you should see "
"grey or black or white on your screen. Many camera profiles violate this "
"\"neutral\" condition. I am not aware of a list of other technical "
"requirements for a suitable working space. However, I can think of another "
"good reason why you wouldn't want to edit your image in your camera profile "
"color space. If you look at the size of a typical camera profile, it is on "
"the order of a quarter to a half a megabyte or more. It's got a lot of "
"information about all the changes that need to be made at different regions "
"of color and tonality in the original scene, to get accurate color rendition "
"from the RGB values that come out of the raw processor. The camera profile "
"is accurate (at least for colors in the original target) but not "
"particularly mathematically smooth. Working space color profiles, on the "
"other hand, are very small in size (half a kilobyte instead of half a "
"megabyte) because they describe a color gamut in terms of smooth, continuous "
"mathematical functions. Working space profiles don't need to make allowances "
"for the \"messiness\" of real world sensors, so the mathematical "
"manipulations performed during image editing will go much more smoothly and "
"accurately than if you try to edit your image while it is still in the "
"camera color space."
msgstr ""
"Nakon svega, profil kamere bi trebao omogućiti najbolje uklapanje boja "
"snimljenih kamerom, s obzirom na moju prozeduru obraderaw-a, zar ne ? "
"Wikipedija kaže, \"Radni prostori, kao što su sRGB ili Adobe RGB, su "
"prostori boja koji olakšavaju dobre rezultete tijekom uređivanja. Na "
"primjer, pikseli sa istom vrijednosti RGB-a bi trebali biti neutralni.\" "
"\"[P]ikseli sa istom vrijednosti RGBa bi trebali biti neutralni\" znači samo "
"da za bilo koji piksel u slici koja je bila prebačena u odgovarajući radni "
"prostor, ako je R=G=B trabali biste vidjeti sivu, crnu ili bijelu na "
"ekranu.  Mnogi profili kamera narušavaju ovaj uslov \"neutralnosti\". Nismo "
"svjesni liste drugih tehničkih  zahtjeva za odgovarajući radni prostor. "
"Međutim, zna se drugi dobar razlog  zašto ne želite uređivati slike u "
"prostoru profila Vaše kamere. Ako pogledate veličinu tipičnog profila "
"kamere, reda veličine je četvrtine ili pola megabajta ili više. Sadrži mnogo "
"informacija o svim promjenama koje treba da se naprave u različitim regijama "
"boje i tonaliteta na originalnoj slici, da bi se dobio precizno izlaganje "
"boje iz RGB vrijednosti koje dolaze iz procesora. Profil kamere je precizan "
"(barem za boje u originalnoj meti) ali ne tako matematički gladak.  Radni "
"profili prostora boja, s druge strane, su veoma mali  u pogledu veličine "
"(pola kilobajta umjesto pola megabajta) zato što opisuju skalu boja u "
"uslovima, glatke, neprekidne matematike funkcije. Profili radnih prostora ne "
"trebaju praviti dozvole  za \"neurednost\" senzora, tako da matematičke "
"manipulacije izvedene tijekom uređivanja slike  će teći glađe i priciznije "
"nego kao kad pokuđate urediti sliku dok je još u prostoru boje kamere."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "Which working space should I choose?"
msgstr "Koji radni prostor da odaberem?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Everyone has an opinion. I'm just going to lay out some of the bits of "
"information needed to make an informed choice. Working space profiles are "
"characterized by:"
msgstr ""
"Svi imaju svoje mišljenje. Iznijećemo neke činjenice koje su važne za "
"donošenje ispravne odluke. Radni prostori su karakterizirani po:"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gamma (or other transfer function), which dictates how much the original "
"linear intensity values captured by the camera sensor (and subjected to the "
"in-camera A-to-D conversion, then interpolated by the raw processing program "
"to produce the image file) are altered to make editing easier or more "
"precise."
msgstr ""
"Gamma (ili drugim prenosnim funkcijama), koje određuju  koliko je originalne "
"linearne vrijedosti, koje je snimio  senzor kamere (i podvrgnute konverziji "
"A-do-D unutar kamere, onda interpolirane programom na obradu raw datoteka "
"zbo ptoizvodnje slike), promijenjeno da bi se olakšalo ili preciziralo  "
"uređivanje."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"RGB primaries which dictate the range of colors, that is, the color gamut, "
"covered by a given profile."
msgstr ""
"RGB primari koji određuju raspon boja, što je, skala boja, pokrivena "
"odrešenim profilom."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"White point (usually D50 or D65 though other values may be used), which "
"specifies the color temperature of the white point of the working space."
msgstr ""
"Bijela tačka (obično D50 ili D65  iako se mogu koristiti i druge "
"vrijednosti), koja određuje temperaturu boje bijele tačke radnog prostora."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "What gamma should my working space have?"
msgstr "Koju gamm-u bi trebao imati moj radni prostor?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The gamma of a color profile dictates what power transform needs to take "
"place to properly convert from an image's embedded color profile (perhaps "
"your working color space or your camera color profile) to another color "
"profile with a different gamma, such as your chosen working space, or the "
"display profile used to display the image on the screen or perhaps from one "
"working space to another, or perhaps from your working space to your "
"printer's color space. Dcraw outputs a 16-bit image with a linear gamma, "
"which means that a histogram of the resulting image file shows the actual "
"amount of light that each pixel on the camera sensor captured during the "
"exposure (paraphrasing <ulink url=\"http://www.guillermoluijk.com/tutorial/"
"dcraw/index_en.htm\">this page</ulink>). (Which is why at present applying a "
"camera profile to the dcraw output also requires applying an appropriate "
"gamma transform to get to the desired working space, unless the camera "
"profile also uses gamma=1.)"
msgstr ""
"Gamma profila boja određuje koja snaga je potrebna za pravilnu konverziju  "
"iz ugrašenog profila slike (ožda Vaš radni prostor ili kamerin radni "
"prostor) u rugi prostor s drugačijom gammom, kao što je Vaš izabrani radni "
"prostor, ili profil za prikazivanje koji se korisi za prikazivanje slika na "
"ekran ili možda iz jednog radnog prostora u drugi, ili možda iz vašeg radnog "
"prostora u printerov. Dcraw proizvodi  16-itnu sliku sa linearnom gammom, "
"što znači da histogram  rezultujuće slike  prikazuje tačnu količinu svjetla  "
"koju svaki piksel  sa senzora kamere snimi tijekom ekspozicije "
"(parafraziranje <ulink url=\"http://www.guillermoluijk.com/tutorial/dcraw/"
"index_en.htm\">ove stranice</ulink>). (Zato tranutna primjena profila kamere "
"na dcraw zahtijava primjenu prikladne gamma transformacije da se dobije "
"željeni radni prostor, osim ako profil kamere koristi gamma=1.)"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One practical consequence of the gamma of a working space is that the higher "
"the gamma, the more discrete tones are available for editing in the shadows, "
"with consequently fewer tones available in the highlights. Changing the "
"gamma of an image redistributes the number of tones available in the lighter "
"and darker areas of an image. Theoretically, if you are working on a very "
"dark-toned (low key) image you might want a working space with a higher "
"gamma. And if you are working on a high key image, say a picture taken in "
"full noon sunlight of a wedding dress with snow as a backdrop, you might "
"want to choose a working space with a lower gamma, so you have more "
"available tonal gradations in the highlights."
msgstr ""
"Jedna praktilna posljedica gamma radnog prostora je da što je veća gamma, "
"diskretniji tonovi su dostupni za uređivanje sjena, sa zbog toga manje "
"dostupnih tonova u nagalašavanju. Promjena gamme na slici preraspodjeljuje "
"broj tonova dostupnih u svjetlijim i tamnijim dijelovima slike. Teoretski, "
"ako radite na slici sa veoma tamnim tonovima možda ćete željeti radni "
"prostor sa većom gammom. A ako radite sa slikom svjetljih tonova, recimo "
"slika uslikana u podne sa bijelom vjenčanicom i snijegom u pozaini, želite "
"izabrati radni prostor sa nižom gammom, tako da imate veću gradaciju tonova."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Theory aside, in the real world of real image editing, almost everyone uses "
"working spaces with either a gamma of either 1.8 or 2.2. sRGB and L*-RGB are "
"two notable exceptions."
msgstr ""
"Teoriju nastranu, u realnosti uređivanja slika, skori svako koristi sa "
"gammom  ili 1.8 ili 2.2 sRGB i L*-RGB su dva primjetna izuzetka."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:64
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "sRGB uses a transfer function close to that of a CRT (and thus not "
#| "necessarily relevant to image editing or to display on an LCD). As "
#| "Wikipedia notes, \"Unlike most other RGB color spaces the sRGB gamma can "
#| "not be expressed as a single numerical value. The overall gamma is "
#| "approximately 2.2, consisting of a linear (gamma 1.0) section near black, "
#| "and a non-linear section elsewhere involving a 2.4 exponent and a gamma "
#| "(slope of log output versus log input) changing from 1.0 through about "
#| "2.3\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SRGB\">this "
#| "page</ulink>), which makes for some complicated math during image "
#| "processing."
msgid ""
"sRGB uses a transfer function close to that of a CRT (and thus not "
"necessarily relevant to image editing or to display on an LCD). As Wikipedia "
"notes, \"Unlike most other RGB color spaces the sRGB gamma can not be "
"expressed as a single numerical value. The overall gamma is approximately "
"2.2, consisting of a linear (gamma 1.0) section near black, and a non-linear "
"section elsewhere involving a 2.4 exponent and a gamma (slope of log output "
"versus log input) changing from 1.0 through about 2.3\" (cited from <ulink "
"url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SRGB\">this page</ulink>), which makes "
"for some complicated math during image processing."
msgstr ""
"sRGB koristi transfernu funkciju blizu CRT (i prema toe ne nužno relevantnu "
"za uređivanje slika ili prikazivanje na LCDu). Ako navodi Wikipedija, \"Za "
"razliku od većine ostalih RGB obojenih prostora sRGB gamma se ne može "
"izraziti kao jedinsvena numerička vrijednost\". Sve u svemu  gamma je "
"probližno 2.2, sadržeći linearni dio (gamma 1.0) u blizini crne, a "
"nelinearni dio drugdje uključujući 2.4 eksponent i gammu(nagib između "
"izlaznog i ulaznog log-a) mijenjajući od 1.0 do 2.3\" (citat sa<ulink url="
"\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SRGB\">ove stranice</ulink>), što čini malo "
"komplikovaniju matematiku kroz obradu slika."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:68
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "L*-RGB uses as its transfer function the same perceptually uniform "
#| "transfer function as the CIELab color space. \"When storing colors in "
#| "limited precision values\" using a perceptually uniform transfer function "
#| "\"can improve the reproduction of tones\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://"
#| "en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_color_space\">this page</ulink>)."
msgid ""
"L*-RGB uses as its transfer function the same perceptually uniform transfer "
"function as the CIELab color space. \"When storing colors in limited "
"precision values\" using a perceptually uniform transfer function \"can "
"improve the reproduction of tones\" (cited from <ulink url=\"https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_color_space\">this page</ulink>)."
msgstr ""
"L*-RGBkoristi kao prenosnu funkciju istu perceptivno uniformnu prenosnu "
"funkciju kao CIELab obojeni prostor. \"Kada pohranjujete boje u ograničenim "
"preciznim vrijednostima\" korištenje perceptivno uniformne prenosne funkcije "
"\"može se poboljšati reprodukcija tonova\" (citat sa <ulink url=\"http://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_color_space\">ove stranice</ulink>)."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to gamma=1.8 and gamma=2.2, the only other gamma for a working "
"space that gets much mention or use is linear gamma, or gamma=1.0. As noted "
"above, dcraw outputs linear gamma files if you ask for 16-bit output. Linear "
"gamma is used in HDR (high dynamic range) imaging and also if one wants to "
"avoid introducing gamma-induced errors into one's regular low dynamic range "
"editing."
msgstr ""
"U dodatku gamma =1.8 i gamma = 2.2, jedina druga gamma za radni prostor koja "
"se mnogo spominje ili koristi je linearna gamma, ili gamma=1.0. Kako je "
"navedeno prije, dcraw  daje linearne gamma datoteke ako tražite 16-bitni "
"izlaz. Linearna gamma se koristi u HDR (visoki dinamički opseg) slikanju i "
"također ako se želi izjeći uvođenje gamma-induciranih  grešaka u regularni "
"niži dinamički opseg uređivanja."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"\"Gamma-induced errors\" is a topic outside the scope of this tutorial. But "
"see \"Gamma errors in picture scaling\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.4p8.com/eric.brasseur/gamma.html\">this page</ulink>) for gamma-induced "
"tonality shifts; and of course see Timo Autiokari's informative (albeit "
"somewhat infamous) website for a whole-hearted endorsement of using linear "
"gamma working spaces (Timo's website seems to be down at present, though "
"archived copies of his articles are still available through google). Bruce "
"Lindbloom mentions a commonly-encountered gamma-induced error that is caused "
"by incorrectly calculating luminance in a nonlinear RGB working space (see "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/index.html?WorkingSpaceInfo.html"
"\">this page</ulink>, sidenote 1). And in a similar vein, the calculations "
"involved in mixing colors together to produce new colors (such as using a "
"digital filter to add warmth to an image) result in gamma errors unless the "
"new colors are calculated by first transforming all the relevant values back "
"to their linear values."
msgstr ""
"\"Gamma inducirane greške\" je tema izvan opsea ovog tutorijala. Ali "
"pogledajte \"Gamma greške u skaliranju slika\" (citat sa <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.4p8.com/eric.brasseur/gamma.html\">ove stranice</ulink>) za gamma "
"inducirano pomijeranje tonova; i naravno pogledajte Timo Autiokari-jevu "
"informativnu web stranicu za svesrdnu podršku korišteja linearnih gamma  "
"radnih prostora(Timo-ina web stranica se čini nedostupna sada, iako su "
"arhivirane kopije njegovih članaka još dostupne preko google-a). Bruce "
"Lindbloom spominje  često susretane gamma inducirane greške  koje su "
"uzrokovane netačnim računanjem svjetline u nelinearnim RGB radnim prostorima "
"(pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/index.html?"
"WorkingSpaceInfo.html\">ovu stranicu </ulink>,sprimjedba 1). I u sličnoj "
"veni, proračuni uključeni u miješanje boja zajedno da se dobiju nove boje "
"(kao što je korištenje digitalnih filtera za dodavanje topline slici) "
"rezultuju gamma greškama osim ako su nove boje izračunate tako šro su prvo "
"transformisane sve relevantne vrijednosti u linearne vrijednosti."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately and despite their undeniable mathematical advantages, linear "
"gamma working spaces have so few tones in the shadows that (in my opinion) "
"they are impossible to use for editing if one is working in 8-bits, and "
"still problematic at 16-bits. When the day comes when we are all doing our "
"editing on 32-bit files produced by our HDR cameras on our personal "
"supercomputers, I predict that we will all be using working spaces with "
"gamma=1. Adobe Lightroom is already using a linear gamma working space "
"\"under the hood\", CS2 allows the option of using linear gamma for mixing "
"colors, and Lightzone has always used a linear gamma working space."
msgstr ""
"Nažalost i uprkos njihovim nepobitnim matematički prednostima, linaerni "
"gamma radni prostori imaju nekoliko tonova u sjenama koje je (prema mom "
"mišljenju) nemoguće urediti ako se radi sa 8 bita, a još je problematičo i "
"sa 16 bita. Kada dođe dan kada budemo svi radili sa 32-bitnim datotekama "
"koje proizvode HDR kamere na našim superkompjuterima, predviđam daćemo "
"koristiti radne prostore sa gammom=1.0. Adobe Lightroom već koristi linearni "
"gamma radni prostor \"ispod haube\", CS2 dozvoljava opciju korištenja "
"linearne gamme za miješanje boja, i Lightzone je uvijek koristio linearni "
"gamma radni prostor."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "How many discrete tonal steps are there in a digital image?"
msgstr "Koliko diskretnih tonskih koraka postoji u digitalno slici?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In an 8-bit image, you have 256 tonal steps from solid black to solid white. "
"In a 16-bit image theoretically you have 65536 steps. But remember, those 16-"
"bits started out as either 10 bits (=1024 steps), 12 bits (=4096 steps), or "
"14 bits (=16384 steps) as produced by the camera's A-to-D converter - the "
"extra bits to reach 16-bits start out as just padding. The available tones "
"are not distributed evenly from light to dark. In linear gamma mode (as the "
"camera sensor sees things), there's a whole lot more tones in the highlights "
"than in the shadows. Hence the advice, if you shoot raw, to \"expose to the "
"right but don't blow the highlights\". See Ron Bigelow's <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.ronbigelow.com/articles/articles.htm\">articles on \"why raw\"</ulink>, "
"for a full discussion of the distribution of available tones in a raw image."
msgstr ""
"U 8-bitnoj slica, imate 256 tonskih koraka od čvrste crne do čvrste bijele. "
"U 16-bitnoj slici teoretski imate 65536 koraka. Ali zapamtite, tih 16 bita "
"počelo je ili kao 10 bita (=1024 koraka), 12 bita (=4096 koraka), ili 14 "
"bita (=16384 koraka) kako su proizvođeni kao kamerini A-do-D konverteri -"
"dodatni biti  za dostizanje 16 bita su samo proširenje. Dostupni tonovi nisu "
"distribuisani jednako od svijetlih do tamnih. U linearnoom gamma načinu "
"(kako senzori kamere vide stvari), postoji mnogo više tonova u naglacima "
"nego u sjenama. Stoga savjet, ako slikate raw, \"izložite na desno ali "
"nemojte pokvariti naglaske\". Pogledajte Ron Bigelow-ove <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.ronbigelow.com/articles/articles.htm\">članke na temu  \"zašto raw\"</"
"ulink>, za cijelu diskusiju o raspodjeli dostupnih tonova u raw slici."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Should I use a large-gamut or a small-gamut working space?"
msgstr ""
"Da li bi trebali koristiti veliku-skalu ili malu-skalu radnog prostora?"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One major consideration in choosing a working space is that some working "
"spaces are bigger than others, meaning they cover more of the visible "
"spectrum (and as a consequence include some imaginary colors - mathematical "
"constructs that don't really exist). These bigger spaces offer the advantage "
"of allowing you to keep all the colors captured by your camera and preserved "
"by the LCMS conversion from your camera profile to the super-wide-gamut "
"profile connection space and out again to your chosen working space."
msgstr ""
"Jedna ogromna stvar koju treba razmotriti pri  izabiru radnog prostora  je "
"da su neki radni prostori veći od drugih, što zanči da pokrivaju veći dio "
"vidjlivog sprektra (a kao posljedicu uključuje i neke imaginarne boje - "
"matematičke konstrukcije koje zapravo ne postoje). Ovi veči prostori nude "
"prednosti omogučavanja zadržavanjavih snimljenih boja  i sačuvanih LCMS "
"konverzijm iz profila kamere u ovaj profil super-široke-skale i ponovo u Vaš "
"odabrani radni prostor."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"But keeping all the possible colors comes at a price, as explained below. "
"And it seems that any given digital image likely only contains a small "
"subset of all the possible visible colors that your camera is capable of "
"capturing. This small subset is easily contained in one of the smaller "
"working spaces (an exception requiring a larger color gamut would be a "
"picture of a highly saturated object such as yellow daffodil)."
msgstr ""
"Ali zadržavanje svih mogućih boja skupo se plaća. Čini se da bilo koja "
"digitalna slika vjerovatno sadrži mali podskup svi mogućih vidljivih boja "
"koje je kamera u mogućnosto snimit. Ovaj mali podskup se lako nalazi u "
"jednom od namanjih radnih prostora (Izuzetak koji zahtijeva veliku skalu "
"boje bila bi slika  jako zasićenog objekta kao što je žuti narcis.)."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:106
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Using a very large working space means that editing your image (applying "
#| "curves, increasing saturation, etc) can easily produce colors that your "
#| "eventual output device (printer, monitor) simply cannot reproduce (you "
#| "cannot see these colors while you're editing, either). So the conversion "
#| "from your working space to your output device space (say your printer) "
#| "will have to remap the out-of-gamut colors in your edited image, some of "
#| "which might even be totally imaginary, to your printer color space with "
#| "its much smaller color gamut. This remapping process will lead to "
#| "inaccurate colors and loss of saturation at best. Even worse, the "
#| "remapping can easily lead to banding (posterization - gaps in what should "
#| "be a smooth color transition, say, across an expanse of blue sky) and "
#| "clipping (e.g your carefully crafted muted transitions across delicate "
#| "shades of red, for example, might get remapped to a solid block of dull "
#| "red after conversion to your printer's color space). Also, the experts "
#| "say that 8-bit images just don't have enough tones to stretch across a "
#| "wide gamut working space without banding and loss of saturation, even "
#| "before conversion to an output space. So if you choose a large gamut "
#| "working space, make sure you start with a 16-bit image."
msgid ""
"Using a very large working space means that editing your image (applying "
"curves, increasing saturation, &etc;) can easily produce colors that your "
"eventual output device (printer, monitor) simply cannot reproduce (you "
"cannot see these colors while you're editing, either). So the conversion "
"from your working space to your output device space (say your printer) will "
"have to remap the out-of-gamut colors in your edited image, some of which "
"might even be totally imaginary, to your printer color space with its much "
"smaller color gamut. This remapping process will lead to inaccurate colors "
"and loss of saturation at best. Even worse, the remapping can easily lead to "
"banding (posterization - gaps in what should be a smooth color transition, "
"say, across an expanse of blue sky) and clipping (&eg; your carefully "
"crafted muted transitions across delicate shades of red, for example, might "
"get remapped to a solid block of dull red after conversion to your printer's "
"color space). Also, the experts say that 8-bit images just don't have enough "
"tones to stretch across a wide gamut working space without banding and loss "
"of saturation, even before conversion to an output space. So if you choose a "
"large gamut working space, make sure you start with a 16-bit image."
msgstr ""
"Korištenje veoma veliko radnog prostora  znači da uređivanjem slike "
"(primjena krivih, povećavanje zasićenja, itd-ž.) lako možete napraviti boju "
"koju mogući uzlazni uređaj (printer ili monitor ) ne može prepoznati  (ne "
"možete vidjeti te boje dok uređujete). Dakle konverzija iz vašeg radnog "
"prostora u  prostor izlanog uređaja (recimo printer) će morati remapirati "
"sve boje izvan opsega u uređenoj slici, od kojih neke mogu biti totalno "
"imaginarne, za prosto printera koji ima mnogo manju skalu.  Ovaj proces "
"remapiranje će voditi nepreciznim bojama i gubitku zasićenja. Čak gore, "
"remapiranje može vodite zapetljanju (posterizacija - praznine u kojima bi "
"trebao biti glatki prelaz, npr nebo) i cijepanju (npr.pažljivo ste napravili "
"prelaze preko osjetljivih nijansi crvene, možda se remapiralio u čvrsti blok "
"masne crvene nakom konverzije u primterov prostor ). Također, eksperti kažu  "
"da 8bitne slike jednostavno nemaju dovoljno tonova da se protegnu preko "
"široke skale radnog prostora bez savijanja i gubitka zasićenja, čak i prije "
"konverzije u izlazni prostor. Ako ste izaraili veliku skali radnogprostora, "
"pobrinite se da počnete sa 16-bitnom slikom."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To summarize, large gamut working spaces, improperly handled, can lead to "
"lost information on output. Small gamut working spaces can clip information "
"on input. Medium-sized gamut working spaces try to strike a happy medium. "
"Like Wikipedia says, it's a trade-off."
msgstr ""
"Zaključak, velika skala radnih prostora, kojima se napravilno rukuje, mogu "
"dovesti do gubitka informacija na izlazu. Mala skala radnih prostora može "
"odsjeći informacije na početku. Skala rednje veličine  pokušava da zadrži "
"zlatnu sredinu. Kao što Wikipedija kaže, sve je na vama."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here are some oft-repeated bits of advice on choosing a working space:"
msgstr "Evo nekoliko često ponavljanih savjeta  za izabir zadnog prostora:"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For images intended for the web, use (or at least convert the final image "
"to) sRGB."
msgstr ""
"Za slike namijenjene iternetu, koristite (ili najmanje konvertujete "
"poljednju sliku) sRGB."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For the most accuracy in your image editing (that is, making the most of "
"your limited \"bits\" with the least risk of banding or clipping when you "
"convert your image from your working space to an output space), use the "
"smallest working space that includes all the colors in the scene that you "
"photographed, plus a little extra room for those new colors you "
"intentionally produce as you edit."
msgstr ""
"Za najpreciznije uređivanje slika (što znači, pravljenje većine ograničenih "
"bita sa rizikom savijanja ili sječenja prilikom konverzije u izlazni "
"prostor ), koristite najmanji radni prostor koji uključuje sve boje sa "
"mjesta slikanja, plus malo dodatnog prostora za nove boje koje napravite "
"tokom uređivanja."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are working in 8-bits rather than 16-bits, choose a smaller rather "
"than a larger working space to avoid clipping and banding."
msgstr ""
"Ako radite u (bitnom radije nego u 16bitnom prostoru, izaberite manji "
"prostor  da izbjegnete gubitke."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For archival purposes, convert your raw file to a 16-bit tiff with a large "
"gamut working space to avoid loosing color information. Then convert this "
"archival tiff to your medium-gamut or large-gamut working space of choice "
"(saving the converted working tiff under a new name, of course)."
msgstr ""
"Za svrhe arhiviranja, prebacite raw datoteku u 16-bitni tiff sa velikom "
"skalom radnog prostora da izbjegnete gubitak informacija o bojama. onda "
"prebacite taj arhivski tiff  u srednju-skalu ili veliku-skalu po ozboru "
"(snimanjem prebačenor radnog tiff pod novim imenom, naravno)."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-cm-wkspace.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on choosing a working space, see <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.brucelindbloom.com/\">this page</ulink>, Information about RGB Working "
"Spaces for a visual comparison of the gamut (array of included colors) of "
"the various working color spaces. See <ulink url=\"http://www.luminous-"
"landscape.com/tutorials/prophoto-rgb.shtml\">here</ulink> and <ulink url="
"\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/sRGB-AdobeRGB1998.htm\">here</"
"ulink> for a pro- and con- presentation, respectively, of the merits of "
"using large gamut working spaces. And while you are on the cambridgeincolour."
"com website, check out the tutorial on color management."
msgstr ""
"Za više informacija o izboru radnog prostora, pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://"
"www.brucelindbloom.com/\">ovu stranicu </ulink>,Informacije o  RGB radnom "
"prostoru za vizualno poređenja skala (niz uključenih boja) različitih radnih "
"prostora. Pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/"
"tutorials/prophoto-rgb.shtml\">ovdje</ulink> i <ulink url=\"http://www."
"cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/sRGB-AdobeRGB1998.htm\">ovdje</ulink> za "
"prezentaciju za i protiv, respektivno, prednosti korištenja radnih prostora "
"velike skale. I dok ste na stranici cambridgeincolour.com, provjerite "
"tutorijal o upravljanju bojama."

#~ msgid "RAW File Treatment and Color Management"
#~ msgstr "Upotreba RAW datoteka i upravljanje bojama"

#~ msgid "Introduction"
#~ msgstr "Uvod"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The point of a color-managed workflow is to ensure that the colors coming "
#~ "from your camera or scanner have a predictable relationship with the "
#~ "colors you actually photographed or scanned, that the colors displayed on "
#~ "your monitor match the colors coming from your camera or scanner, and "
#~ "that the colors you print or display on the web match the colors you "
#~ "produced in your digital darkroom."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Namjena grafika toka za upravljene bojama je da omogući da boje koje "
#~ "dolaze sa vaše kamere ili skenera imaju predvidivu vezu sa bojama koje "
#~ "ste zapravo uslikali ili skenirali, da boje koje se prikazuju na vašem "
#~ "monitoru odgovaraju bojama koje dolaze sa kamere ili skenera  da boje "
#~ "koje printate ili prikazujete na internetu odgovaraju bojama koje ste "
#~ "izabrali pri obradi fotografija."

#~ msgid "Which buttons do I push?"
#~ msgstr "Koju dugmad da pritisnem?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "When it comes to color management, everyone wants to know, \"which "
#~ "buttons do I push to get the results I want\". Unfortunately, color "
#~ "management of necessity involves making informed choices at every step "
#~ "along the image-processing workflow. The purpose of this tutorial is to "
#~ "provide sufficient background information on color management, along with "
#~ "links to more in-depth information, to enable you to begin to make your "
#~ "own informed decisions, based on your own desired results."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kada je riječ o upravljanju bojama, svi se pitaju \"koju dugmad da "
#~ "pritisnem da dobijem očekivani rezultat?\". Nažalost,  upravljanje bojama "
#~ "nužno uključuje donošenje važnih odluka pri svakom koraku kroz cijelu "
#~ "obradu fotografije. Svrha ovog uputstva je da omogući dovoljno "
#~ "informacija o upravljanju bojama, zajedno sa linkovima sa dubljim "
#~ "informacijama i omogući Vam da donosite  vaše odluke zasnovane na "
#~ "željenim rezultatima."

#~ msgid "Is there anyone who doesn't need to worry about color management?"
#~ msgstr "Da li postoji neko ko ne bi trebao da brine o upravljanju bojama?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If your imaging workflow meets all six criteria listed below, then you "
#~ "don't need to worry about color management."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako vaš tok rada sa slikama uključuje svih šest kriterija navedenih "
#~ "ispod, onda ne trebate da brinete o upravljanju bojama."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "you are working at a monitor properly calibrated to the sRGB color space "
#~ "(more about that below)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "radite na monitoru ispravno kalibrisanom za sRGB prostor boja (više o "
#~ "ovome navedeno je ispod)"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "your imaging workflow starts with an in-camera-produced jpeg already in "
#~ "the sRGB color space"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "vaš tok rada sa slikama počinje sa u-kameri-proizvedenim jpeg-om koji je "
#~ "već u sRGB prostoru boja"

#~ msgid "you work exclusively in the sRGB color space for editing"
#~ msgstr "radite isključivo u sRGB prostoru boja za uređivanje"

#~ msgid "your printer wants images in the sRGB color space"
#~ msgstr "vaš printer zahtjeva slike u sRGB prostoru boja"

#~ msgid "your scanner produces images in the sRGB color space"
#~ msgstr "vaš skener daje slike u sRGB prostoru boja"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "your only other image output is via email or the web, where sRGB is the "
#~ "de facto standard"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "vaš jedini način slanja fotografija je email ili internet, gdje je sRGB "
#~ "zapravo standard"

#~ msgid "The sRGB color space"
#~ msgstr "SRGB prostor boja"

#~ msgid "What is so special about the sRGB color space?"
#~ msgstr "Šta je tako posebno u sRGB prostoru boja?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "sRGB is widely accepted as a standard color profile by virtually everyone "
#~ "involved with consumer-oriented imaging. sRGB was proposed in 1996 by "
#~ "Hewlett Packard and Microsoft as a standardized color space for consumer-"
#~ "oriented applications. As stated in the initial HP/MS proposal: "
#~ "<blockquote><para>Hewlett-Packard and Microsoft propose the addition of "
#~ "support for a standard color space, sRGB, within the Microsoft operating "
#~ "systems, HP products, the Internet, and all other interested vendors. The "
#~ "aim of this color space is to complement the current color management "
#~ "strategies by enabling a third method of handling color in the operating "
#~ "systems, device drivers and the Internet that utilizes a simple and "
#~ "robust device independent color definition. This will provide good "
#~ "quality and backward compatibility with minimum transmission and system "
#~ "overhead. Based on a calibrated colorimetric RGB color space well suited "
#~ "to Cathode Ray Tube (CRT) monitors, television, scanners, digital "
#~ "cameras, and printing systems, such a space can be supported with minimum "
#~ "cost to software and hardware vendors...</para></blockquote> "
#~ "<blockquote><para>Currently, the ICC [International Color Consortium]... "
#~ "tracks and ensures that a color is correctly mapped from the input to the "
#~ "output color space... by attaching a profile for the input color space to "
#~ "the image in question. This is appropriate for high end users. However, "
#~ "there are a broad range of users that do not require this level of "
#~ "flexibility and control. Additionally, most existing file formats do not, "
#~ "and may never support color profile embedding, and finally, there are a "
#~ "broad range of uses [that] actually discourage people from appending any "
#~ "extra data to their files. A common standard RGB color space addresses "
#~ "these issues ... by merging the many standard and non-standard RGB "
#~ "monitor spaces into a single standard RGB color space. Such a standard "
#~ "could dramatically improve the color fidelity in the desktop environment. "
#~ "For example, if operating system vendors provide support for a standard "
#~ "RGB color space, the input and output device vendors that support this "
#~ "standard color space could easily and confidently communicate color "
#~ "without further color management overhead in the most common situations. "
#~ "(<ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org/Graphics/Color/sRGB\">archived copy</"
#~ "ulink>)</para></blockquote> To summarize, the point of the by-now almost "
#~ "universally adopted sRGB color space was and is to make life easier for "
#~ "consumers (no need to worry about color management), less expensive for "
#~ "manufacturers (no need to worry about compatibility between consumer-"
#~ "level digital cameras or scanners, monitors, printers, and so forth), and "
#~ "more convenient for displaying images on the Internet (don't worry about "
#~ "embedding and reading icc profiles - just assume sRGB)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "sRGB su većinom  prihvatili kao standard za boje, svi koji su uključeni u "
#~ "korisnički usmjerenu obradu fotografija. sRGB su prvi put predstavili "
#~ "1996 Hewlett Packard i Microsoft kao stndardizovani prostor boja za "
#~ "korisnički orjentisane aplikacije. Kako je navedeno u HP/MS prijedlogu :  "
#~ "<blockquote><para> Hewlett-Packard i Microsoft dodatak podrške za "
#~ "standardni prostor boja, sRGB, kroz Microsoft.ove operativne sisteme, HP."
#~ "ove proizvode, Internet, i sve druge zainteresovane prodavače. Cilj ovog "
#~ "prostora boja je da upotpuni  trenutne strategije upravljanja bojama, "
#~ "omogućavajući  treću metodu  podržavanja boja u operativnim sistemima, "
#~ "drajverima i Internetu koji koriste jednostavne a snažne uređaje "
#~ "nezavisnih definicija boja. Ovo će omogućiti dobru kvalitetu i pozadinsku "
#~ "kompatibilnost sa minimumom prenosa i višim sistemom. Zasnovan na "
#~ "kalibrisanom kolorimetrijskom  RGB prostoru boja, koji dobro pristaje u "
#~ "monitore sa katodnom cijevi (CRT), televizore, skenere, digitalne kamere, "
#~ "i printere, kao  prostori mogu biti podržani sa minimalnim troškovima za "
#~ "softver i hardver prodavače... </para></blockquote> <blockquote><para> "
#~ "Trenutno ICC [Međunarodni konzorcijum za boje] prato i osigurava da su "
#~ "boje pravilno mapirane iz ulaznoog do izlaznog prostora... kačeći  profil "
#~ "za ulazni prostor na sliku u pitanju. Ovo je pogodno za sofisticirane "
#~ "korisnike. Međutim, postoji mnogo korisnika koji ne zahtijevaju ovaj nivo "
#~ "fleksibilnosti i kontrole. Dodatno, najčešći formati  ne podržajavu, i "
#~ "nikad neće podržavati ugrađivanje boje profila, i konačno, postoji mnogo "
#~ "upotreba koje zapravo obeshrabriju korisnike da dodaju bilo kakve nove "
#~ "podatke u svoje datoteke. Trenutno standard RGB prostor oja navodi "
#~ "sljedeće probleme... ujedinjujući mnoge standardne i ne-standardne  RGB "
#~ "prostore ekrana u jedan standardni  RGB prostor boja. Ovak standard bi "
#~ "mogao dramatično poboljšati tačnost  u desktop okruženju. Na primjer, ako "
#~ "bi prodavač operativnih sistema omogućili podršku RGB standarda prostora "
#~ "boja, proizvođači ulaznih i izlaznih uređaja koji podržavaju ovaj "
#~ "standard mogli bi jednostavno i samopouzdano komunicirati bojama bez "
#~ "dodatnog upravljanja bojama  u običnim situacijama.(<ulink url=\"http://"
#~ "www.w3.org/Graphics/Color/sRGB\">archived copy</ulink>)</para></"
#~ "blockquote> Da zaključimo, cilj do sada skoro univerzalnog sRGB prostora "
#~ "boja bio je i još uvijek jeste da olakša korisnicima (bez brige za "
#~ "upravljanjem bojama), manje troškova za proizvođače(bez brige o "
#~ "kompatibilnosti između korisničkih digitalnih kemera ili skenera,  "
#~ "monitora, printera itd.), i  mnogo prikladniji za prikazivanje slika na  "
#~ "Internetu (bez brige o ugrađivanju i čitanju ICC profila - samo se "
#~ "pretpostavi sRGB)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "So if sRGB works so well and makes life so easy for everyone, why use any "
#~ "other color space and thus be forced to worry about color management "
#~ "issues?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako je sRGB tako dobar i svima toliko olakšava, zašto koristiti prostor "
#~ "boja i tako se prisiljavati  na brigu oko upravljanja bojama?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "sRGB was designed to contain colors easily displayed on consumer-oriented "
#~ "monitors and printed by consumer-oriented printers manufactured in 1996. "
#~ "This least-common-denominator set of viewable and printable colors - the "
#~ "technical term is \"color gamut\" - is much smaller than the set of "
#~ "colors we can see in the real world, much smaller than the set of colors "
#~ "today's digital cameras can capture, much smaller than the set of colors "
#~ "today's printers can print, and much smaller than the color gamut of the "
#~ "new wide gamut monitors that are beginning to enter the consumer market. "
#~ "For anyone who wants to make use of the wider color gamuts available "
#~ "today even at the consumer level, the gamut of sRGB is too small. "
#~ "Conversely, if you don't intend to make use of an expanded gamut of "
#~ "colors at any point in your digital imaging workflow, then you don't need "
#~ "to worry about non-sRGB color spaces and all the attending intricacies of "
#~ "color management."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "sRGB je dizajniran da sadrži boje koje se lako prikazuju na korisnički "
#~ "orjentisanim monitorima i printerima proizvedenim 1996. Ovaj najmanje "
#~ "čest skup nazivnika boja koje je moguće vidjeti i printati - tehnički "
#~ "naziv je \"skala boja\" - je mnogo manji nego skup boja koje možemo "
#~ "vidjeti u stvarnom svijet, mnogo manji od skupa boja koje današnje "
#~ "digitalne kamere mogu zabilježiti, mnogo manji od skupa boja koje "
#~ "današnji printeri mogu isprintati, i mnogo manji od skale boja novih "
#~ "širokih ekrana koji počinju da se pojavljuju na korisničkom tržištu. Za "
#~ "svakoga ko želi da koristi veće skale boja dostupne dana čak i na "
#~ "korisničkom nivou, skala sRGBa je jako mala. Suprotno, ako ne namjeravate "
#~ "da koristite proširenu skalu boja u bilo kojem trenutku vašeg rada sa "
#~ "obradom digitalnih fotografija, onda ne treba dabrinete i ne sRGB "
#~ "prostorima boja i svim tim zamršenostim upravljanja bojama."

#~ msgid "How small is sRGB?"
#~ msgstr "Koliko mali je sRGB?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A visual representation of the limitations of sRGB compared to the colors "
#~ "we actually see in the real world is presented here after. It shows a two-"
#~ "dimensional representation of all the colors we can see (the horseshoe-"
#~ "shaped region) and the colors contained in the sRGB space (the smaller "
#~ "triangular region)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Vizuelna reprezentacija ograničenja sRGB-a u poređenju sa bojama koje "
#~ "zapravo vidimo  je prezentovano ovdje. Pokazuje dvodimenzionalnu "
#~ "reprezentaciju svih boja koje možemo vidjeti (regija u obliku potkovice) "
#~ "i bojja sadržanih u sRGB-u (manja trpugaona regija)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If you would like to see a two-dimensional representation of sRGB "
#~ "compared to some of the larger working color spaces, see Bruce "
#~ "Lindbloom's excellent <ulink url=\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/\">site</"
#~ "ulink>, click on \"Info\" then on \"Information About RGB Working Spaces"
#~ "\"."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako želite da vidite dvodimenzionalnu reprezentaciju sRGB-a u poređenju "
#~ "sa većim radnim prostorima boja, pogledajte Bruce Lindbloomovu odličnu "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/\">stranicu</ulink>, kliknite "
#~ "na  \"Info\" a zatim na \"Information About RGB Working Spaces\"."

#~ msgid "Calibrating and profiling your monitorRGB?"
#~ msgstr "Kalibracija i profajliranje RGB monitora."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If I choose to work exclusively in the sRGB color space, do I need to "
#~ "calibrate my monitor?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako izaberem da radim samo u sRGB radnom prostotu boja, da li treba da "
#~ "kalibriše monitor?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Yes! Whether you stay within the color gamut provided by sRGB or not, you "
#~ "need a properly calibrated monitor because sRGB assumes that your monitor "
#~ "is calibrated to sRGB. Your monitor calibration closes the loop. If you "
#~ "work within the color gamut provided by sRGB then you need to calibrate "
#~ "your monitor to the sRGB standard (or produce and use an accurate monitor "
#~ "profile, or both)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "DA! Bez obzira da li ostajete pri skali boja koju osigurava sRGB iline, "
#~ "morate pravilno kalibrisati monitor zato što aRGBpretpostavlja da je vaš "
#~ "monitor kalibrisan za sRGB. Kaliracija vašeg monitora zatvara petlju. Ako "
#~ "radite unutar skale boja koju osigurava sRGB onda morate da kalibrišete "
#~ "Vaš monitor na sRGB standard (ili proizvesti i koristiti precizan profil "
#~ "monitora, ili oboje)."

#~ msgid "What are the consequences of working with an uncalibrated monitor?"
#~ msgstr "Koje u posljedice rada sa nekalibrisanim monitorom?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are several possible consequences, none of them good. Every "
#~ "monitor, calibrated or otherwise, has a native (uncalibrated) white "
#~ "point, expressed as a temperature in degrees Kelvin. The white point of a "
#~ "monitor (calibrated or not) is the color you see when you are looking at "
#~ "a patch of pure white on your screen. Pure white is when the RGB values "
#~ "in your image all equal 255 (as expressed in 8-bits), such as the plain "
#~ "white background of a web page or an office document. You are thinking, "
#~ "\"white is white\" but if you were able to line up several monitors "
#~ "calibrated to different white points, you would see that the higher the "
#~ "temperature of the monitor's white point, the bluer the screen looks in "
#~ "comparison with monitors with lower white points. If you can find the "
#~ "controls of your own monitor, change the temperature up and down "
#~ "(remembering to put it back to its initial setting when you are done, "
#~ "unless you decide you want a different white point). Your eyes, which "
#~ "adapt quickly to a constant white point, will easily discern the screen "
#~ "getting bluer and yellower as you move the white point higher and lower. "
#~ "If your uncalibrated monitor is too blue (native CRT color temperature is "
#~ "typically 9300K and sRGB assumes 6500K), as you edit your image you will "
#~ "overcompensate and produce images that will look yellowish and too warm "
#~ "on a properly calibrated monitor. Conversely, if your monitor is too "
#~ "yellow because the color temperature is set too low (I believe LCD native "
#~ "color temperature is around 5500K), your images will look blueish/too "
#~ "cool on a properly calibrated monitor."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoji nekoliko posljedice, sve loše.Svaki monitor, kalibrisan ili "
#~ "drugačije, ima matičnu (nekalibrisan) bijelu tačku, izraženu kao "
#~ "temperatura u stepenia Kelvina. Bijela tačka monitora (kalibrisan ili ne) "
#~ "je boja koju vidite kada gledate u dio čiste bijele na vašem ekranu. "
#~ "Čista bijela je kada su sve RGB vrijednosti u vašoj slici jednake "
#~ "255(izraženo na 8 bita),kao što je bijela podloga web stranica ili word-"
#~ "ovog dokumenta. Vi mislite, bijelo je bijelo, ali ako ste imali priliku "
#~ "da poredate nekoliko monitora kalibrisanih na različite bijele tačke, "
#~ "vidjeli biste da što je veća temperatura bijele tačke monitora, ekran je "
#~ "plavlji u odnosu na druge monitore sa nižim bijelim tačkama. Ako možete "
#~ "pronaći kontrole Vašeg monitora, promijenite temperaturu gore i dolje "
#~ "(zapamtite da je vratite na početne postavke kada završite, osim ako ste "
#~ "odlučili  da želite drugačiju bijelu tačku). Vaše oči, koje se "
#~ "prilagođavaju brzo na konstantnu bijelu tačku , lako će razaznati ekran "
#~ "koji postaje plavlji i žući  kako mičete bijelu tačku više i niže. Ako "
#~ "Vaš nekalbrisani monitor je previše plavi (matičnaCRT temperatura bije je "
#~ "tipično 9300K i sRGB se pretpostavlja na 6500K), kako uređujete sliku "
#~ "nadoknadićete i proizvesti slike koje će izgledati žućkasto i pretoplo na "
#~ "pravilno kalibrisanom monitoru. Obratno, ako je Vaš monitor previše žut  "
#~ "zbog temperature boje koja je preniska (Vjerujem da je matična boja  LCDa "
#~ "oko 5500K), Vaše slike  će izgledat plavkast/ prehladno na pravilno "
#~ "kalibrisanom monitoru."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Setting a proper white point is only part of monitor calibration. You "
#~ "also need a proper black point, brightness (luminance), and gamma "
#~ "(transfer) function. If your monitor is too dark because the black point "
#~ "is set too low, you will overcompensate and produce images that look "
#~ "washed out on a properly calibrated monitor. Conversely, if your monitor "
#~ "black point is set too high, your images will look took dark and overly "
#~ "saturated on a properly calibrated monitor."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postavljanje odgovarajuće bijele tačke je samo dio kaliracije monitora. "
#~ "Također trebate pravilnu crnu tačku, svjetlinu, i gamma (prenosnu) "
#~ "funkciju. Ako je Vaš monitor pretaman zbog toga što je crna tačka "
#~ "premala. nadoknadićete i proizvesti slike koje izgledaju izaprano  na "
#~ "pravilno kalibrisanom monitoru. Obratno, ako je crna tačka vašeg monitora "
#~ "previsoka, Vaše slike će izgledati pretamno i prezasićeno na pravilno "
#~ "kalirisanom monitoru."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If the brightness/contrast is set too high, you will assume your images "
#~ "have a lot more \"pop\" than they really have when viewed on a properly "
#~ "calibrated monitor, plus your eyes will hurt and your LCD screen will "
#~ "burn out faster."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako je svjetlina/kontrast previsok, pretpostavićete da Vaše slike imaju "
#~ "previše \"pop-a\" nego na pravilno kalibrisanom monitoru, plus će Vas "
#~ "boljeti oči i LCD ekran će se prije istrošiti."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If your monitor gamma is improperly set, your tonal variations from dark "
#~ "to light will be off. That is, the shadows or highlights might be overly "
#~ "compressed or expanded, leading you to compensate in the opposite "
#~ "direction. So when viewed on a properly calibrated monitor, the shadows "
#~ "might be too bright or dark (or the highlights too dark or bright), with "
#~ "the rest of the image suffering from tonal over-compression. And heaven "
#~ "help you if the internal R, G, and B guns (or LCD equivalent) of your "
#~ "monitor are improperly set (each gun has its own black point and gain), "
#~ "because the resulting color casts - too green, too magenta, too orange, "
#~ "etc, that you will inevitably create by \"correcting\" your image during "
#~ "editing - are very obvious when viewed on a properly calibrated monitor."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako je gamma Vašeg monitora nepravilno postavljena, Vaše varijacije "
#~ "tonova od tamnih do svijetlih neće postojati. To je zog toga, što sjene i "
#~ "naglasci mogu biti kompresovani ili prošireni, vodeći Vas ka kompenzaciji "
#~ "u suprotnom smjeru. Tako da kada pregledate na pravilno kalibrisanom "
#~ "monitoru, sjene će možda biti presvijetle ili pretamne ( ili sa ostatkom "
#~ "slike i je naglasak pretaman ili presvijetao), sa ostatkom slike koja "
#~ "pati od preopterećenja tonova. Bog Vam pomogao ako su unutrašnji R,G i B "
#~ "pištoljji (ili LCD ekvivalenti) vašeg monitora nepravilno postavljeni "
#~ "(svaki pištolj ima svoju vlastitu crnu tačku i dobit), zato što su  "
#~ "rezultujuća pretvaranja boja - previše zeleno, previše purpurnocrvena, "
#~ "previše narandžasta, etc, koje ćete neizbježnno kreirati \"ispravljajući"
#~ "\" slike tijekom uređivanja -   očita kada se gleda na pravilno "
#~ "kalibrisanom monitoru."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Whether or not your monitor is properly calibrated, you might be "
#~ "surprised by the results of comparing an image you've edited on your home "
#~ "monitor to the same image as displayed by other monitors in your house or "
#~ "on your friend's and neighbor's monitors. We certainly were - we have two "
#~ "Sony Trinitron monitors in our home, one with a failing (too high) green "
#~ "gun and one with a failing (too high) blue gun. Every image edited on "
#~ "either monitor looked very wrong on the other monitor, until we purchased "
#~ "a spectrophotometer to calibrate and profile both monitors. "
#~ "Unfortunately, at this point neither of these two monitors can be "
#~ "calibrated to display a proper black point, so they are no longer used "
#~ "for image editing - the point being that an additional benefit of using a "
#~ "spectrophotometer is you know when it's time replace your monitor."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Bilo da je Vaš monitor pravilno kalibrisan ili ne, možda ćete se "
#~ "iznenaditi rezultatom upoređivanja slike koju ste uredili na monitoru kod "
#~ "kuće sa istom slikom koja je  se prikazuje na drugim monitorima u Vašoj "
#~ "kući ili kod Vašeg prijatelja. Mi smo zasigurno bili - imamo dva Sony "
#~ "Trinitron monitora u kući, jedan sa propalim (previsokim) zelenim "
#~ "pištoljem a jedan sa propalim (previsokim ) plavim pistoljem. Svaka slika "
#~ "uređena na bilo kojem od ovih monitora  je izgledala pogrešno na ovom "
#~ "drugom, dok nismo nabavili spektrofotometar za kalibrisanje i "
#~ "profajliranje oba monitora. Nažalost, u ovom trenutku nijedan od ovih "
#~ "monitora se ne može kalibrisati da prikazuje pracilnu crnu tačku, tako da "
#~ "oni više ne mogu koristiti za uređivanje slika - poenta je dodatna "
#~ "povlastica korištenja spektrofotometra na osnovu koje možete znati kada "
#~ "je vrijeme da zamijenite monitor."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The meaning of \"black point\" and \"brightness\" seems pretty clear, but "
#~ "what does \"gamma\" mean?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Značenje \"crne tačke\" i  \"svjetline\" se čini jasno, ali šta znači "
#~ "\"gamma\"?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "See <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_correction\">this "
#~ "Wikipedia article</ulink> for an overview of the role of gamma in "
#~ "monitors and photography; the links at the bottom of the article are all "
#~ "excellent sources of additional information. Wikipedia says \"Gamma "
#~ "compression, also known as gamma encoding, is used to encode linear "
#~ "luminance or RGB values into video signals or digital video file values; "
#~ "gamma expansion is the inverse, or decoding, process ... Gamma encoding "
#~ "helps to map data (both analog and digital) into a more perceptually "
#~ "uniform domain.\" Yeah, I know, clear as mud. Read the Wikipedia article "
#~ "and study the pictures. Eventually it will sink in. If you wade very "
#~ "deeply into image editing and color management, eventually you will need "
#~ "to make decisions about what gamma (or other encoding/decoding function) "
#~ "you want to use when you calibrate your monitor, profile your digital "
#~ "camera, and choose a working color space. When in doubt (for those of you "
#~ "who just want to know which button to push!), gamma=2.2 is a widely-used "
#~ "value, both for monitor calibration and working color spaces."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Pogledajte ovaj <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_correction"
#~ "\">Wikipedia članak</ulink> za pregled uloge gamma-e u monitorima i "
#~ "fotografiji; linkovi na dvu članka su odlični izvori dodatnih "
#~ "informacija. Wikipedia kaže \"Gamma kompresija, također poznata kao gamma "
#~ "kodiranje, se koristi da se kodiraju linearna svjetlina ili RGB "
#~ "vrijednosti u video signale; gamma širenje je inverzno, ili dekodiranje, "
#~ "proces...\" Gama kodiranje pomaže u mapiranju  podataka (i digitalnih i "
#~ "analognih) u uniformniji domen.\" Da znam, jasno ko dan.  Pročitajte "
#~ "Wikipedjin članak i proučite slike. Vremenom će potonuti. Ako se zarovite "
#~ "duboko u uređivaje slike i upravljanje bojama, vremenom ćete  morati "
#~ "donijeti odluke o tome koju gamma-u želite (ili drugu funkciju kodiranja/"
#~ "dekodiranja) da koristite kada kalibrišete Vaš monitor, profajlirate "
#~ "digitalnu kameru, i izaberete prostor i radnu boju. Kada se dvoumite (za "
#~ "one koji samo želite da znate koje dugme da pritisnete!), gamma=2.2 je "
#~ "široko rasprostranjena, i za kalibraciju monitora i za obojene radne "
#~ "prostore."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "What's the difference between calibrating a monitor and profiling a "
#~ "monitor?"
#~ msgstr "Koja je razlika između kalibracije i profajliranja monitora?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "When first learning about color management, many people are confused "
#~ "about the difference between calibrating and profiling a monitor (I know "
#~ "I was). Quoting from Hal Engel's excellent discussion in the &digikam; "
#~ "users forum:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kada prvi put uče o upravljanju bojama, mnogi ljudi su zbunjeni razlikama "
#~ "kalibracije i profajliranja monitora(barem ja jesam). Citat iz Hal Engels-"
#~ "ove odlične diskusije na forumu za korisnike &digikam;a:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Calibration is a process where a device is brought into some defined "
#~ "state by making adjustments to its controls or some other physical means. "
#~ " For example, the act of calibrating a monitor involves adjusting its "
#~ "white point, black level, luminosity and gamma to predetermined or "
#~ "standard values using the monitor's controls and by altering the video "
#~ "card gamma ramp... In contrast to calibration, the process of creating a "
#~ "profile is a characterization of the device that does not involve making "
#~ "any changes or adjustments to the device. Rather it is a measurement "
#~ "process that results in a file that contains a precise mathematical "
#~ "description of the device's color and tonality characteristics. This file "
#~ "is an ICC profile. These characteristics include the transfer function "
#~ "from the device's color space to a standardized absolute color space "
#~ "(this is called a Profile Color Space, PCS, in an ICC profile), the "
#~ "device's white point, black point, primaries and other information. "
#~ " Displays are normally characterized (profiled) in their calibrated "
#~ "state. To summarize, calibration makes changes to the device to alter "
#~ "it's color reproduction characteristics to conform to some predetermined "
#~ "state.   Profiling or characterization is a measurement process that "
#~ "results in a detailed description of the device's (normally calibrated) "
#~ "color reproduction characteristics. (cited from <ulink url=\"http://"
#~ "digikam.1695700.n4.nabble.com/Re-Color-Managed-View-How-td1739136."
#~ "html#a14160285\">here</ulink>)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kalibracija je proces u kojem se uređaj dovodi u neko definisano stanje "
#~ "prilagođavanjem njegovih kontrola ili nekih drugih fizičkih dijelova.   "
#~ "Na primjer, čin kalibracije monitora uključuje prilagođavanje bijele "
#~ "tačke, nivoa crna, svjetline i gamma-e za unaprijed određene ili "
#~ "standardne vrijednosti koristeći kontrole monitor i izmjenu video kartice "
#~ "gamma platforme... Subrotno kalibraciji, proces pravljenja profila je "
#~ "karakterizacija uređaja koji ne uključuje pravljenje izmjena ili "
#~ "prilagođavanje uređaja.   To je najprije proces mjerenja koji rezultuje "
#~ "datotekom koja sadrži precizne matematičke opise boje uređaja i "
#~ "karakteristike tonova.   Ovaj datoteka je ICC profil.   Ove "
#~ "karakeristike  uključuju funkciju prebacivanja sa obojenog prostora "
#~ "uređaja  na standardizovani apsolutni obojeni prostor (ovo se zove "
#~ "Profilni obojeni prostor, PCS, u ICC profilu), bijelu tačku uređaja, crnu "
#~ "tačku, primarne i druge informacije.    Dipleji su normaln "
#~ "karakterizovani (profajlirani ) u svom kalibrisanom stanju. Da "
#~ "rezimiramo, kalibracija pravi promjene na uređaju da izmijeni njegove "
#~ "karakteristike reprodukcije boje da se prilagodi  nekim predodređenim "
#~ "stanjima.   Profajliranje ili karakterizacija je mjerni proces koji "
#~ "rezultuje detaljnim opisom karakteristika reprodukcije boje "
#~ "uređaja(normalno kalibrisanog).  (citat preuzet  <ulink url=\"http://"
#~ "digikam.1695700.n4.nabble.com/Re-Color-Managed-View-How-td1739136."
#~ "html#a14160285\">odavde</ulink>)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Calibrating your monitor technically is not really part of color "
#~ "management. But obviously a properly calibrated and/or profiled monitor "
#~ "is a prerequisite for a color-managed workflow. This tutorial does not "
#~ "cover the important topics of how to calibrate and profile a monitor. The "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.argyllcms.com/\">ArgyllCMS </ulink> and <ulink "
#~ "url=\"http://lprof.sourceforge.net/\">LProf </ulink> documentations are "
#~ "very good and highly recommended reading. To use either of this software "
#~ "to calibrate and/or profile your monitor, you will need a "
#~ "spectrophotometer. A spectrophotometer (sometimes called a \"spider\") is "
#~ "a device for measuring the RGB values of color patches projected onto the "
#~ "monitor screen by calibration/profiling software such as Argyll and "
#~ "LProf. The Argyll website maintains an up-to-date list of supported "
#~ "spectrophotometers. I believe LProf can use all the spectrophotometers "
#~ "that Argyll can use, as the two programs share the relevant sections of "
#~ "code."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kalibracija vašeg monitora tehnički nije dio upravljanja bojama. ali "
#~ "očigledno pravilno kalibrisan mobitel i/ili profajliran monitor je "
#~ "preduslov za bojom-upravljan radni tok. Ovaj tutorijal ne pokriva vvađne "
#~ "teme o tome kako pravilno kalibrisati monitor. <ulink url=\"http://www."
#~ "argyllcms.com/\">ArgyllCMS </ulink> i <ulink url=\"http://lprof."
#~ "sourceforge.net/\">LProf </ulink> dokumentacija je veoma dobra i jako "
#~ "preporučena za čitanje. Da koristite jedan od ovih softvera za "
#~ "kalibraciju i/ili profajlliranje Vašeg monitora, trebaćete "
#~ "spektrofotofmetar. Spektrofotometar (ponekad se zove i \"pauk\") je "
#~ "uređaj za mjerenje RGB vrijednosti sloja boje  koje  kalibracijski/"
#~ "profajlerski softveri kao što su Argyll i LProf projektuju  na ekran "
#~ "monitora. Web stranica Argyll-a održava nadogradivu listu podržani "
#~ "spektrofotometara. Vjerujem da LProf može koristiti sve spektrofotometre "
#~ "kao i Argyll, kako ova dva programa dijele najvažnije dijelove koda."

#~ msgid "Can I calibrate my monitor without a spectrophotometer?"
#~ msgstr "Može li se monitor kalibrisati bez spektrofotometra?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are various methods given on the Internet for calibrating a monitor "
#~ "without using a spectrophotometer. These \"eye-ball\" methods are better "
#~ "than not calibrating your monitor at all, and depending your eyeball and "
#~ "your monitor, can produce quite usable results. But the eye-ball methods "
#~ "are not a substitute for a properly calibrated and profiled monitor. For "
#~ "the record, calibrating and profiling a monitor with a spectrophotometer, "
#~ "though intimidating at first, is not difficult. Spectrophotometers can be "
#~ "obtained for well under $100 US (if you opt for a more expensive model, "
#~ "make sure you are paying for a better piece of hardware, rather than just "
#~ "a more fully-featured accompanying bit of manufacturer's software that "
#~ "won't run under Linux). Argyll and/or LProf documentation will guide you "
#~ "through the process of calibrating and profiling your monitor, without "
#~ "your having to learn very much color management theory. And if/when you "
#~ "learn enough about color management to realize that you want or need a "
#~ "more detailed monitor profile of a particular type, for a particular "
#~ "purpose, these two softwares have all the advanced capabilities you could "
#~ "possibly hope for."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoji više različitih metodana internetu za kalibraciju monitora bez "
#~ "spektrofotometra. Ove metode\"od-oka\"su bolje od nekalibrisanog "
#~ "monitora, a u zavisnosti od vašeg vida i monitora, mogu se dobiri "
#~ "iskoristivi rezultati. Ali ove metode od-oka nisu zamjena za pravilnu "
#~ "kalibraciju iprofajliranje monitora. Za zapisnik, kalibracija i "
#~ "profajliranje monitora sa spektrofotometrom, iako zastrašujuće na prvu, "
#~ "nije uopće teško. Spektrofotometri se mogu nabaviti za manje od $100 US "
#~ "(ako izaberete skuplji model, pobrinite se da plaćate za bolji hardverski "
#~ "dio, nego za samo sotver sa vise mogućnosti  koji neće raditi na Linuxu). "
#~ "Argyll i/ili LProf dokumentacija  će Vas voditi kroz proces kalibracije i "
#~ "profajlirannja  monitora, a nećete morati naučiti mnogo teorije u "
#~ "upravljanju bojama. A ako/kada naučite dovoljno o upravljanju bojama da "
#~ "shvatiite da želite ili trebate detaljniji profil monitoraodređenog tipa, "
#~ "za određene svrhe, ova dva softvera imaju sve napredne mogućnosti kojima "
#~ "biste se mogli nadati."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Assuming I've decided to work exclusively in the sRGB color space, what "
#~ "\"&digikam; buttons\" should I push after I calibrate my monitor?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Pretpostavljajući da sam odlučio/la da samo radim u sRGB prostoru boja, "
#~ "koja \"&digikam; dugad\" treba da pritisnem nakon kalibracije monitora?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If your monitor has been calibrated to the sRGB standard and you work "
#~ "exclusively in the sRGB color space, then you can disable color "
#~ "management in digikam. You don't need to tell &digikam; what monitor "
#~ "profile to use because &digikam; defaults to using the sRGB color space "
#~ "as the monitor color space profile. And you don't need to tell &digikam; "
#~ "to use a color-managed workflow because &digikam; defaults to using sRGB "
#~ "for your camera, printer, and working space, just as laid out by HP and "
#~ "MS back in 1996."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako je Vaš monitor kalibrisan na sRGB standard a radite samo u sRGB "
#~ "obojeneom prostoru, onda možete onemogućiti upravljanje bojama u "
#~ "digikamu. Ne morate reći &digikam;u koji profil monitora da koristi zato "
#~ "što &digikam; koristi sRGB obojeni prostor kao monitorov obojeni profil. "
#~ "I ne morate reći &digikam;i da koristi bojama upravljan radni tokzato što "
#~ "&digikam; koristi sRG za Vašu kameru, printer, i radni protor, samo kao "
#~ "postavku HPa i MS iz 1996."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "But if you want to take the first steps toward a color-managed workflow, "
#~ "then refer to <ulink url=\"help:/digikam/using-setup.html#setup-"
#~ "iccprofiles\">corresponding page of Settings</ulink>, enable color "
#~ "management, and select sRGB as your monitor profile, your camera profile, "
#~ "your working space profile, and your printer profile. If you've also used "
#~ "Argyll or LProf to produce a monitor profile after you calibrated your "
#~ "monitor - perhaps named \"mymonitorprofile.icc\" - then tell &digikam; to "
