#~ msgid ""
#~ "Does the lighting and wall/ceiling/drape/furniture colors near my monitor "
#~ "matter?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Da li imaju uticaja osvjetljenje i boja zida/plafona/zavjese/namještaja "
#~ "pored mog monitora?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Yes! Good lighting is a prerequisite for proper image editing and for "
#~ "comparing prints to the image on your screen. If the lighting near your "
#~ "workstation is too bright, colors on your monitor look too dark, and "
#~ "conversely. If the light from the fixtures in your workroom have a low "
#~ "CRI (color rendering index, meaning you don't have full spectrum bulbs), "
#~ "or if the light in your workroom comes from a window and so varies as the "
#~ "weather and time of day varies (or worse, is filtered through colored "
#~ "drapery), or if the walls and ceiling are creating color casts on your "
#~ "monitor, then your editing process will \"correct\" color casts that "
#~ "don't really exist. Best advice, as far as is consistent with maintaining "
#~ "harmony in the family: neutral grey walls and ceiling, cover the windows, "
#~ "wear neutral clothing, set appropriate light levels using appropriate "
#~ "bulbs and fixtures. For more information on what are the appropriate "
#~ "light levels, bulbs and fixtures for editing images and viewing prints, "
#~ "see the following articles:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "DA! Dobro osvjetljenje je preduslov za pravilo uređivanje slika i za "
#~ "upoređivanje isprintanih sa slikama na vašem ekranu. Ako je osvjetljenje "
#~ "blizu Vašeg radnog prostora prejako, boje na vašem monitoru će izgledati "
#~ "pretamne, i obratno. Ako svjetlo u vašoj radnoj sobi ima nizak CRI "
#~ "(indeks vraćanja boja, to znači da nemate sijalice punog spektra), ili "
#~ "ako svjetlo u vašoj radnoj sobi dolazi sa prozora i tako varira u "
#~ "zavisnosti od vremena i doba dana (ili gore, ako se filtrira kroz obojene "
#~ "zavjese), ili ako zidovi i plafon mijenjaju boje koje stižu do monitora, "
#~ "onda će Vaš proces uređivanja \"ispraviti\" boje koje zapravo ne postoje. "
#~ "Najbolji savjet, dok je konzistentan sa održavanjem harmonije  u "
#~ "porodici: neutralno sivi zidovi i plafon, pokrijte prozore, nosite "
#~ "neutralnu odjeću, postavite prikladno svjetlo  koristeći  prikladne "
#~ "sijalice za više informacija o prikladnim nivoima svjetlosti, sijalicama "
#~ "za uređivanje slika i pregledanje isprintanih, pogledajte sljedeće članke:"

#~ msgid "The camera profile and issues with raw file development"
#~ msgstr "Profil Kamere i problemi sa razvojem raw datoteka"

#~ msgid "What's the next step in color management?"
#~ msgstr "Koji je sljedeći korak u upravljanju bojama?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "First and for the record, many excellent professional and amateur "
#~ "photographers save all their images as in-camera jpegs and work "
#~ "exclusively in the sRGB color space. But if you want to work in a larger "
#~ "color space, or if you want to work with raw files (even if you output "
#~ "sRGB image files from your raw files), read on."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Prvo, nogo odličnih fotografa profesionalaca i amatera čuvaju njihove "
#~ "slike kao unutar kamere jpeg-ove i rade isključivo sa sRGB obojenim "
#~ "prostoreom. Ako ako želite da radite u većem obojenom prostoru, ili ako "
#~ "želite da radite sa raw datotekama (čak i ako prebacite sRGB slike iz raw "
#~ "datoteka), nastavite čitati."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Judging from questions asked in the &digikam; user's forum, if you are "
#~ "reading this tutorial you probably are shooting raw images with a digital "
#~ "dSLR and you are hoping that somewhere in the arcane waters of color "
#~ "management lies the answer to how to get a nice picture from your raw "
#~ "image file. And you're right! The next thing you need is the right camera "
#~ "profile for developing your raw image. But first let's answer the "
#~ "question you really might have been asking:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Sudeći prema postavljenim pitanjima na forumu &digikam; korisnika, ako "
#~ "čitate ovo uputstvo vjerovatno snimate raw slike sa digitalnim dSLR-om i "
#~ "nadate se da se negdje u tajanstvenim vodama upravljanja bojama krije "
#~ "odgovor na pitanje kako dobiti lijepu sliku iz raw slike. Upravu ste! "
#~ "Sljedeće stvar koju trevate jeodgovaraući profil kamere za razvoj raw "
#~ "slika. Ali prvo odgovorimo  na pitanje koje ste možda stvarno pitali:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Why doesn't the image produced by raw converters like dcraw or ufraw look "
#~ "like the embedded preview displayed by digikam?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Zašto slike proizvedene raw konverterom kao što je  dcraw ili ufraw "
#~ "izgledaju kao ugrađeni pregled digikama?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Glad you asked. All digital camera images start out as raw files, whether "
#~ "or not the camera allows the user the option to save the image as a raw "
#~ "file. When you ask the camera to save jpegs instead of raw files, the "
#~ "camera uses its on-board processor to convert the raw file to a jpeg. "
#~ "That embedded preview is what your final image would have looked like if "
#~ "you had set your camera to save jpegs instead of raw files."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Drago nam je da ste pitali? Sve slike digitalnih kamera počinju kao raw "
#~ "datoteke, bez obzira da li kamera podržava korisničku opciju snimanja "
#~ "slike kao raw datoteke. Kada pitate kameru da smini jpeg umjesto raw "
#~ "datoteke, ona koristi ugraćeni procesor za pretvaranje iz raw i jpeg. Taj "
#~ "ugrađeni pregled je ono kako bi vaša slika izgledala da postavite vaš "
#~ "kameru da snima jpeg-ove umjesto raw datoteka."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "From here I will speak from my experience as a Canon user, but I will "
#~ "guess that most or all entry-level and mid-range dSLRs behave in a "
#~ "similar manner. Canon offers the user several picture styles - neutral, "
#~ "standard, portrait, landscape, and so forth - that determine what kind of "
#~ "processing will be done to the raw image file to produce the final image, "
#~ "whether or not the processing is done \"in-camera\" or later, using the "
#~ "proprietary Canon DPP software. The Canon DPP raw processing software "
#~ "does give the user additional control, but still manipulates the raw "
#~ "image file in accordance with the chosen picture style. Most of the Canon "
#~ "picture styles add a heavy S-curve and extra color saturation to give the "
#~ "picture more \"pop\". Even if you choose the \"neutral\" picture style "
#~ "(the Canon picture style that gives you the least modified tonality); and "
#~ "select \"less contrast\", \"less saturation\", \"no noise reduction\", "
#~ "and \"no sharpening\" in the DPP raw development dialog, you will find, "
#~ "if you know what to look for, that an S-curve and also shadow denoising "
#~ "has been applied to your image."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Odsada ću govoriti iz svog iskustva kao Canon korisnik, ali "
#~ "pretpostavljam da se većina ili svi dSLR-ovi ulaznog nivoa i srednjeg "
#~ "omjera ponašaju slično. Canon nudi korisniku nekoliko stilova slikanja, "
#~ "neutralni, standardni, portret, pejzaž, itd - što određuje koji način "
#~ "obrade će se primijeniti na raw datoteke za proizvodnju finalne slike, "
#~ "bez obzira da lije je obrada izvrešena unutar ili izvan kamere, koristeći "
#~ "odgovarajući Canon DPP softver. Canon DPP softver  ne daje korisniku "
#~ "dodatne kontrole, ai još uvijem manipuliše raw slikama u skladu sa "
#~ "izabranim načinom slikanja. Večina Canon stilova slikajna dodaju tešku S-"
#~ "krivu i dodatno zasićenje boje da se slici da veći \"pop\". Čak i ako "
#~ "izaberete \"neutralni\" stil slikanja (Canon stil slikanja daje Vam  "
#~ "najmanje modifikovani tonalitet) i izaberete \"manji kontrast\",\" manje "
#~ "zasićenje\" i bez \"izoštravanja\" u DPP raw razvojnom dijalogu, naći "
#~ "ćete, ako znate šta da tražite, da je S-kriva kao i uklanjanje uke "
#~ "primijenjeno na sliku."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Dcraw (which &digikam; uses to convert raw files to image files) doesn't "
#~ "add an S-curve to your image tonality. Dcraw gives you the lights and "
#~ "darks that are actually recorded by the camera sensor. According to "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://21stcenturyshoebox.com/essays/scenereferredworkflow."
#~ "html\">Tindeman</ulink>, an excellent read and source of good advice, "
#~ "with links to equally good sources of additional information), dcraw is "
#~ "one of only a handful of raw developers that actually gives you the "
#~ "\"scene-referred\" tonality. Ufraw also produces a scene-referred image "
#~ "by default (although ufraw gives the user the option to modify the scene-"
#~ "referred image by changing the tonal distribution and saturation). And "
#~ "the dcraw/ufraw scene-referred image IS flat-looking, because the camera "
#~ "sensor records light linearly, whereas our eyes are constantly "
#~ "interacting with our brain to accommodate dim and bright areas in a "
#~ "scene, meaning our brain to some extent \"applies an S-curve\" to the "
#~ "scene to enable us to better focus in on the areas of particular interest "
#~ "as we look around"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Dcraw (kojeg &digikam; koristi za koverziju raw datoteka u slike) ne "
#~ "dodaje S-krivu na tonalitet Vaše slike. Dcraw Vam daje svjetloću i tamu "
#~ "koje je stvarno sniomo senzor kamere. Prema <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://21stcenturyshoebox.com/essays/scenereferredworkflow.html"
#~ "\">Tindeman</ulink>-u, odličan za čitanje i izvor dobrih savjeta, sa "
#~ "vezama prema jednako dobrim izvorima dodatnih informacija, dcraw je jedan "
#~ "jedini od pregršt raw razvijača koji Vam stvarno daje tonalitet \"u "
#~ "odnosu na scene\". Ufraw takožer proizvodi  slike u odnosu na scene (iako "
#~ "ufraw daje korisniku opciju da izmijeni sliku o odnosu na scenu "
#~ "mijenjajući raspodjelu tonova i zasićenja). Dcraw/ufraw slike u odnosu na "
#~ "scene izledaju ravno, zato što senzori kamere snimaju crveno svjetlo "
#~ "linearno, kako su naše oči  kontantno u interakciji sa mogom "
#~ "prilagođavajući tamna i svijetla područja na sceni, što znači da naš "
#~ "mozak na neke opsege \"primjenjuje S-krivu\" na scenu da nam omogući "
#~ "bolji fokus napodručja određenog interesa  kako gledamo okolo."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The embedded jpeg preview looks so much nicer than dcraw's output. What "
#~ "is the value in scene-referred tonality?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ugrađeni jpeg pregled  izgleda  mnogo ljepše nego dcraw izlaz. Koja je "
#~ "vrijednost tonaliteta u odnosu na scene?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "When you take a picture, presumably you have an idea of what you want the "
#~ "final image to look like.  It is much easier to achieve that final image "
#~ "if you don't have to \"undo\" stuff that has already been done to your "
#~ "image.  Once Canon (or Nikon, or Bibble, or etc) has applied their "
#~ "proprietary S-curves and shadow-denoising, sharpening, etc to your image, "
#~ "then your shadows, highlights, edge detail, etc, are already squashed, "
#~ "clipped, chopped, and otherwise altered and mangled.  You've thrown "
#~ "information away and you cannot get it back.  Especially in the shadows, "
#~ "even with 16-bit images (actually, 12- or 14-bits, depending on the "
#~ "camera, but it's encoded as 16-bits for the computer's convenience), "
#~ "there just isn't that much information to begin with."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kada uslikate sliku, vjerovatno imate ideju  šta želite kao finalni "
#~ "proizvod.   Lakše je postići finalnu sliku ako nemate opciju \"poništi\" "
#~ "koja je već primjenjivana na sliku.   Jednom kad Canon(ili Nixon, ili "
#~ "Bibble i sl.) prmjeni  odgovarajuće S-krive i uklanjanje buke i sjene, "
#~ "izoštravanje na Vaše slike, tada su Vaše sjene, naglasci, ivični detalji, "
#~ "itd, svinuti, podrezani, isječeni ili na drugi način promijenjeni.  "
#~ "Bacili ste informacije i ne možete ih dobitti nazad.   Posebno kod sjena, "
#~ "čak i sa 16-bitnin slikama (zapravo, 12-ili 14-bitnim, u zavisosti od "
#~ "kamere, ali kodiranim na 16 bita zbog praktičnosti kompjutera), "
#~ "jednoostavno ne postoji toliko mngo informacija za početak."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "It seems to me that the heart and soul of image processing is the "
#~ "deliberate manipulation of image tonality, color, selective sharpening, "
#~ "and so forth, such that the viewer focuses in on what you, the "
#~ "photographer, found of particular interest when you took the picture. Why "
#~ "give the art of image processing over to some proprietary raw processing "
#~ "software? In other words, \"flat is good\" if you'd rather give your "
#~ "images your own artistic interpretation.  The alternative is to let the "
#~ "canned, proprietary algorithms produced by Canon, Nikon, Bibble, etc "
#~ "interpret your images for you.  (On the other hand, there is no denying "
#~ "that for many images, those canned algorithms are really pretty good!)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Čini mi se da srce i duša obrade slike   je namjerna manipulacija "
#~ "tonalitetom slike, bojom, selektivnim izoštravanjem, itd, tako da se "
#~ "posmatrač fokusira na to što Vi, fotograf, smatrate cilljnim interesom "
#~ "kada slikate. Zašto dati umjetnost obrade slike nekim određenim "
#~ "softverima za obradu raw datoteka? Drugim riječima, \"ravno je dobro\" "
#~ "ako biste radije dali svojim slikama vlastitu umjetničku interpretaciju.  "
#~ "  Alternativa je da dopustite kozervativnim, korisničkim algoritmima koje "
#~ "su proizveli Canon, Nixon, Bibble itd, da interpretuju vaše slike.    (S "
#~ "druge strane, nema poricanja da su za mnoge slike ti konzervativni "
#~ "algoritmi veoma dobri!)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Well, that's all very interesting. I can see the value in starting my "
#~ "image-editing with a scene-referred rendition instead of the eye-popping "
#~ "rendition that I see in the embedded jpeg. But I'm telling you, the "
#~ "images produced by digikam/dcraw look really really bad! Why?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Dakle, sve je to jako interesantno. Mogu vidjeti vrijednosti pri "
#~ "pokretanju uređivanja slika sa izlaganjem u odnosu na scene umjesto  "
#~ "nevjerovatnog izlaganja  koje ja vidim u ugrađenom jpegu. Ali kažem Vam, "
#~ "slike koje prizvede digikam/dcraw izgledaju jako jako  loše! Zašto?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Well, that depends. If the image looks very dark, then you asked dcraw to "
#~ "output a 16-bit file and you have run into a problem with dcraw not "
#~ "applying a gamma transform before outputting the image file. You can use "
#~ "imagemagick to apply the appropriate gamma transform to the image file "
#~ "produced by dcraw. Or you can find or make a camera profile with a gamma "
#~ "of 1. Or you can use ufraw, which applies the gamma transform for you."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Dakle, zavisi od više faktora. Ako slike izgleda jako tamno, onda ste "
#~ "tražli od dcraw-a da izbac 16-bitnu datoteku  i naišli ste na problem jer "
#~ "dcraw ne primjenjuje gamma transformaciju pri izbacivanja slike. Možete "
#~ "koristiti ImageMagick da primijenite prikladnu gamma transformaiju na "
#~ "slike koje je prizveo dcraw. Ili možete naći ili napravit profil camere "
#~ "sa gammom 1. Ili možete koristiti ufraw, koji primjenjuje gamma "
#~ "transformaciju za Vas."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If your image has pink highlights, there's a solution. For an explanation "
#~ "of the problem, along with the command line cure for this problem, see "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/forum/index.php?"
#~ "topic=23430.0\">this \"Luminous Landscape\" forum post</ulink>."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako vaša slika ima roze naglaske, postoji rješenje. Za objašnjenje "
#~ "problema, zajedno sa lijekom komandnom linjom za ovaj problem, pogledajte "
#~ "ovaj <ulink url=\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/forum/index.php?"
#~ "topic=23430.0\"> \"Luminous Landscape\" post sa foruma</ulink>."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If the image isn't dark but it looks really weird, probably you made some "
#~ "injudicious choices in the digikam/dcraw user-interface. The digikam/"
#~ "dcraw interface conveniently allows you to \"dial in\" options that you "
#~ "would otherwise have to specify at the command line. However, convenience "
#~ "always comes at a price. First, the interface might not provide access to "
#~ "all the options that are available at the command line (as of &digikam; "
#~ "0.9.4, only some of the dcraw command line options are available from the "
#~ "interface). And second, to get the most from the digikam/dcraw interface, "
#~ "you have to know what the buttons, sliders, etc in the interface actually "
#~ "do. Which means you need to know what happens at the command line if you "
#~ "want to get the best results from using the interface. (This tutorial "
#~ "will not attempt to document how to use the digikam/dcraw user interface. "
#~ "Digikam is developing at a rapid pace and anything I might write about "
#~ "the digikam/dcraw interface will surely be outdated in the near future.)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako slika nije tamna ali izgleda veoma čudno, vjerovatno te napravili "
#~ "neke nepromišljene izbore u digikam/dcraw korisničkom  interfejsu. "
#~ "Digikam/dcraw interfejs Vam prikladno dozvoljava da \"pozivate\" opcije "
#~ "koje bste inače morali specifikovati u komndnoj liniji. Međutim, "
#~ "prikladnosti uvijek ima svoju cijenu. Prvo, interfejsmožda neće osigurati "
#~ "pristup svim opcijaa koje su dostupne na komandnoj liniji (od &digikam;a "
#~ "0.9.4, samo neke dcraw opcije komandne linije su dostupne iz interfejsa). "
#~ "Drugo, da dobijete većinu iz digikam/dcraw interfejsa, morate znati šta "
#~ "dugmat, klizači i drugo rade u interfejsu. Što znači da morate znati šte "
#~ "se dešava u komandnoj liniji ako želite da dobijete najbolje rezultate "
#~ "koristeći interfejs. (Ovaj tutorijal  neće pokušati dokumentovati kako "
#~ "koristiti digikam/dcraw korisnički interfejs). Digikam se razvija velikom "
#~ "brzinom i bilo šta što napišem o upotrebi ovih programa će sigurno biti "
#~ "beskorisno u bližoj budućnosti."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For example, if your embedded jpeg has very nice deep rich shadows but "
#~ "the digikam/dcraw-produced jpeg or tiff has blotchy red line patterns in "
#~ "the shadow areas, then you probably put an \"x\" in the \"Advanced, Black "
#~ "point\" option, with the slider set to 0. Uncheck the Black point box and "
#~ "try again. This box in the digikam/dcraw interface corresponds to the \"-k"
#~ "\" option when using dcraw at the command line. The \"-k\" option allows "
#~ "you to override dcraw's best estimate of where, in the shadow tones of "
#~ "your image, does digital signal start to override background noise. If "
#~ "you don't use the \"-k\" option at the command line, then dcraw "
#~ "calculates an appropriate value for you, based on its estimate of "
#~ "background noise. For my Canon 400d/xti, the dcraw-calculated background "
#~ "noise value is usually around 256 (the command line option \"-v\" will "
#~ "tell dcraw to tell you what it's doing as it processes your raw file). "
#~ "If, however, I use the \"-K /path to blackframe.pgm\" option to tell "
#~ "dcraw to subtract out a black frame, then dcraw will report the black "
#~ "point as \"0\", as there is now no need to set it higher to avoid the "
#~ "deepest shadows in the image, where noise typically drowns out signal. (A "
#~ "\"black frame\" is an exposure taken with the lens cap on, with the same "
#~ "exposure settings as, and ideally right after, taking the image being "
#~ "processed. The \"-K\" option allows dcraw to subtract background noise "
#~ "from the image.)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Na primjer, ako vaš ugrađeni jpeg ima veoma lijepe duboke bogate sjene "
#~ "ali jpeg ili tiff koji je proizveo digikam/dcraw ima zamrljane crvene "
#~ "linije u područijma sjena, onda ste vjerovatno stavili \"x\" u "
#~ "\"Napredno, crna tačka\" opciju, sa klizačem postavljenim na 0. Odznačite "
#~ "kučicu Crna tačka i pokupajte ponovo. Ova opcija u digikam/dcraw-u "
#~ "odgovara \"-k\" opciji na komandnoj liniji, onda dcraw računa prikladnu "
#~ "vrijednost za Vas, zasnovanu na procijenjenoj pozadinskoj buki. Za moju "
