#~ msgid ""
#~ "How do I apply a camera profile to the 16-bit image file produced by my "
#~ "open source raw processing software?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kako primjenjujem profil kamere na 16-bitnu sliku koju je proizveo moj  "
#~ "otvoreni softver za obradu raw-a?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If you are using the digikam/dcraw interface, <ulink url=\"help:/digikam/"
#~ "using-setup.html#setup-iccprofiles\">here</ulink> is how to tell "
#~ "&digikam; which camera profile to use. If you are using dcraw from the "
#~ "command line, you have the choice of outputting your 16-bit image file "
#~ "with or without the camera profile already applied. If you ask dcraw to "
#~ "output the file without applying the camera profile, you can use LCMS's "
#~ "tifficc utility (also at the command line) to apply the camera profile. "
#~ "The advantage of using tifficc is that you can tell LCMS to use high "
#~ "quality conversion (dcraw seems to use the LCMS default medium). The "
#~ "disadvantage, of course, is that applying your camera profile from the "
#~ "command line adds one extra step to your raw workflow. If you are using "
#~ "ufraw, consult the ufraw user's guide."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako koristite digikam/dcrawaplikaciju , <ulink url=\"help:/digikam/using-"
#~ "setup.html#setup-iccprofiles\">ovdje </ulink> se nalazi kako reći "
#~ "&digikam;u  koji profil kamere da koristi. Ako koristite dcraw iz "
#~ "komandne linije, onda imte izbor  izlaza 16 bitne datoteke sa ili bez "
#~ "primjene profila kamere. Ako pitate dcraw za izlaz datoteke bez primjene "
#~ "profila , možete koristiti LCMS tiff-ovu mogućnost (također iz komandne "
#~ "linije) primjene profila kamere. Prednost korisštenja tiffika je da "
#~ "možete reči LCMS-u da koristi  visoko kvallitetnu konverziju (čini se da "
#~ "dcraw koristi srednje kvalitetnu). Nedostatak, naravno ja primjena "
#~ "profila kamere iz komandne linije dodaje još jedan korak u radni tok.Ako "
#~ "koristite ufraw, konsultujte ufraw-ove korisničke upute."

#~ msgid "The PCS: color profiles point to real colors in the real world"
#~ msgstr "PCS: profili boja naspram boja u stvarnom svijetu"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Camera, scanner, working space, monitor, printer - what do all these "
#~ "color profiles really do?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kamre, skener, radni prostor, monitor, printer - šta svi ovi profili boja "
#~ "zapravo rade?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A color profile describes the color gamut of the device or space to which "
#~ "it belongs by specifying what real color in the real world corresponds to "
#~ "each trio of RGB values in the color space of the device (camera, "
#~ "monitor, printer) or working space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Profil boje opisuje skalu boje uređaja ili prostora kojem pripada "
#~ "specificirajući koja stvarna boja iz stvarnog sijeta odgovara svakom triu "
#~ "vrijednosti  u obojenom prostoru uređaja (kamera, monitor, printer) ili "
#~ "radnom prostoru."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The camera profile essentially says, \"for every RGB trio of values "
#~ "associated with every pixel in the image file produced from the raw file "
#~ "by the raw processing software, \"this RGB image file trio\" corresponds "
#~ "to \"that real color as seen by a real observer in the real world\" (or "
#~ "rather, as displayed on the IT8 target if you produced your own camera "
#~ "profile, but it amounts to the same thing - the goal of profiling your "
#~ "camera is to make the picture of the target look like the target)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Profil kamere esencijalno kaže, \"za svaki RGB trio vrijednosti\" povezan "
#~ "sa svakim pikselom u slici koji je proizveden iz raw datoteke, \"ovaj RGB "
#~ "tri slike\" odgovara \"realnoj boji koju vidi realan posmatrač u realnom "
#~ "svijetu\" (ili radije, kako je prikazana na IT8 meti ako ste napravili "
#~ "vlastiti profil kamere, ali teži istoj stvari -cilj profajliranja je da "
#~ "se napravi slika meta koja izgleda kao meta)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "You cannot see an image by looking at its RGB values. Rather you see an "
#~ "image by displaying it on a monitor or by printing it. When you profile "
#~ "your monitor, you produce a monitor profile that says \"this RGB trio of "
#~ "values that the graphics card sends to the screen\" will produce on the "
#~ "screen \"that real color as seen by a real observer in the real world\"."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ne možete vidjeti sluku gledajući RAW vrijednosti.Radije pogledajte sliku "
#~ "prokazjući je na ekranu ili je isprintajte. Kako profajlirate monitor, "
#~ "proizvodite profil koji kaže \"ovaj trio RGB vrijednosti koje grafička "
#~ "kartica šalje na ekran\" će na ekranu proizvesti \"tu stvarnu boju koju "
#~ "vidi stvarni posmatrač u stvarnom svijetu\"."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "What the monitor profile and the camera profile have in common is the "
#~ "part (in italics above) about \"that real color as seen by a real "
#~ "observer in the real world.\" Different trios of RGB numbers in, "
#~ "respectively, the monitor and camera color spaces point to the same real, "
#~ "visible color in the real world. Real colors in the real world provide "
#~ "the reference point for translating between all the color profiles your "
#~ "image will ever encounter on its way from camera to screen to editing "
#~ "program to print or the web."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ono što profil mmonitora i profil kamere imaju zajedničko je \" stvarna "
#~ "boja koju vidi stvarni posmatrač u stvarnom svijetu\". Različiti trio-i "
#~ "RGB brojeva u, respektivno, obojenim prostorima  monitora i kamere "
#~ "pokazuju na istu, stvarnu, vidljivu boju u stvarnom svijetu. Stvarne boje "
#~ "u stvarnom svijetu omogućavaju  referentnu tačku  za prenos između svih "
#~ "profila boja koje su vaše slike srele na putu od  ekrana kamere do "
#~ "programa za uređivanje ili interneta."

#~ msgid "How can a color profile point to a real color in the real world?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Kako profil boje moe pokazivati na stvarnu boju u stvarnom svijetu ?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Real people don't even see the same colors when they look at the world, "
#~ "do they?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Stvarni ljudi  čak ni ne vide iste boje kada pogledaju svijet, zar ne?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A long time ago (1931, although refinements continue to be made), the "
#~ "International Color Consortium decided to map out and mathematically "
#~ "describe all the colors visible to real people in the real world. So they "
#~ "showed a whole bunch of people a whole bunch of colors and asked them to "
#~ "say when \"this\" color matched \"that\" color, where the two visually "
#~ "matching colors were in fact produced by differing combinations of "
#~ "wavelengths. What was the value of such a strange procedure? Human color "
#~ "perception depends on the fact that we have three types of cone receptors "
#~ "with peak sensitivity to light at wavelengths of approximately 430, 540, "
#~ "and 570 nm, but with considerable overlap in sensitivity between the "
#~ "different cone types. One consequence of how we see color is that many "
#~ "different combinations of differing wavelengths of light will look like "
#~ "\"the same color\"."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Prije mnogo vremena (1931, iako se prave poboljšanja), Međunarodni "
#~ "konzorcijum boja odlučio je mapiratii i matematički opisati sve boje "
#~ "vidljive stvarnim ljudima u stvarnom svijetu. Tako da su oni pokazali "
#~ "gomili ljudi gomilu boja i pitali ih da kažu kada se \"ova\" boja poklapa "
#~ "sa \"onom\" bojom, gdje su zapravo dvije vizualno iste boje proizvedene "
#~ "različitim kombinacijama talasnih dužina. Kakva je vrijednost tako čudnog "
#~ "postupka?Zapažanje boja kod ljudi zavisi od  činjenice da postoje tri "
#~ "tipa konusnih receptora sa maksimuom osjetljivosti na talasne dužine "
#~ "približno 430, 540, i 570 nm, ali sa preklapanjem u osjetljivosti između "
#~ "dvije konusne vrste. Jedna posljedica toga kako vidimo boje   je da mnoge "
#~ "različite kombinacije različitih  talasnih dužina svjetlosti će izgledati "
#~ "kao \"ista boja\"."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "After extensive testing, the ICC produced the CIE-XYZ color space which "
#~ "mathematically describes and models all the colors visible to an ideal "
#~ "human observer (\"ideal\" in the sense of modeling the tested responses "
#~ "of lots of individual humans). This color space is NOT a color profile in "
#~ "the normal sense of the word. Rather it provides an absolute \"Profile "
#~ "Connecting Space\" (PCS) for translating color RGB values from one color "
#~ "space to another. (See <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
#~ "Tristimulus#Tristimulus_values\">here</ulink> and <ulink url=\"http://en."
#~ "wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_vision\">here</ulink>.)"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Nakon obimnog testiranja, ICC je proizveo CIE-XYZ  prostor boja koji "
#~ "atematički opisuje i modelira sve boje vidljive idalnom čovjeku "
#~ "(\"idealnom\" u smislu  modelranja i testiranja reakcija mnogo "
#~ "pojedinaca). Ovaj prostor boja NIJE profil u pravom smislu te riječi. "
#~ "Prije osigurava apsolutni \"Prostor povezivanja profila\" (PCS) za "
#~ "prevođenje RGB vrijednosti boje  iz jednog prostora boje u drugi. "
#~ "(pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
#~ "Tristimulus#Tristimulus_values\">ovdje</ulink> i <ulink url=\"http://en."
#~ "wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_vision\">ovdje</ulink>. )"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "CIE-XYZ is not the only PCS. Another commonly used PCS is CIE-Lab, which "
#~ "is mathematically derived from the CIE-XYZ space. CIE-Lab is intended to "
#~ "be \"perceptually uniform\", meaning \"a change of the same amount in a "
#~ "color value should produce a change of about the same visual importance"
#~ "\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_color_space"
#~ "\">Wikipedia article</ulink>). Wikipedia says \"The three coordinates of "
#~ "CIELAB represent the lightness of the color (L* = 0 yields black and L* = "
#~ "100 indicates diffuse white; specular white may be higher), its position "
#~ "between red/magenta and green (a*, negative values indicate green while "
#~ "positive values indicate magenta) and its position between yellow and "
#~ "blue (b*, negative values indicate blue and positive values indicate "
#~ "yellow)\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
#~ "Lab_color_space\">Wikipedia article</ulink>)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "CIE-XYZ nije jedini PCS.Drugi često korišteni PCS je CIE-Lab, koi je "
#~ "matematički izveden iz CIE-XYZ prostora. CIE-Lab je namijenjen da bude "
#~ "\"perceptivno jedinstven\", što znači \"promjena iste količine "
#~ "vrijednosti bjoje bi trebala proizvesti promjenu iste vizualne vrijednosti"
#~ "\" (citat iz <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_color_space"
#~ "\">Wikipedijnog članka</ulink>). Wikipedija kaže \"Tri koordinate CIELAB "
#~ "prestavljaju  svjetlinu boje (L* = 0 prinosi crnu a L* = 100 ukazuje na "
#~ "difuznu bijelu; reflektujuća bi možda bila više), poziciju između "
#~ "purpurnocrvene i zelene(a*, egativne vrijednosti ukazuju na zelenu dok "
#~ "pozitivne vrijednosti ukazuju crvenu) i poziciju između žute i bijele "
#~ "(b*, negativne vrijednosti ukazuju na plavu, dok poziitvne ukazuju na "
#~ "žutu)\" (citat iz  <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
#~ "Lab_color_space\">Wikipedijnog članka</ulink>)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "To be useful, color profiles need to be coupled with software that "
#~ "performs the translation from one color space to another via the PCS. In "
#~ "the world of linux open source software (and also many closed source, "
#~ "commercial softwares), translation from one color space to another "
#~ "usually is done by <ulink url=\"http://www.littlecms.com/\">LCMS</ulink>, "
#~ "the \"little color management software\". For what it's worth, my own "
#~ "testing has shown that LCMS does more accurate color space conversions "
#~ "than Adobe's proprietary color conversion engine."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Da budu korisni, profili boja treba da se udruže sa softverom koji "
#~ "obavlja translaciju iz jednog prostora u drugi putem PCS-a. U svijetu "
#~ "linux otvorenih softvera (i mnogo zatvorenih izvora, komercijalnih "
#~ "sotfvera), translacija iz jednog u drugi prostor se obično radi <ulink "
#~ "url=\"http://www.littlecms.com/\">LCMS</ulink>om, \"malim softverom za "
#~ "upravljanje bojama\". Za ono što vrijedi, moja testiranja su pokazala da "
#~ "LCMS radi mnogo preciznije konvezije iz prostora u prostor nego Adobe-ov "
#~ "program."

#~ msgid "Printer profiles, rendering intents, and soft-proofing"
#~ msgstr "Profili printera, svrhe vraćanja, i soft-proofing"

#~ msgid "Where do I get a printer profile?"
#~ msgstr "Gdje mogu dobiti profil printera?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Whew! We've come a long way - almost ready to print that image! Where do "
#~ "I get a printer profile? Well, you already know the answer. You can use "
#~ "the generic profile that comes with your printer. You can purchase a "
#~ "professionally produced profile. If you ask, some commercial printing "
#~ "establishments will send you their printer profiles (which won't work "
#~ "with your printer!). You can make your own printer profile using Argyll, "
#~ "in which case your profile can be tailored to your particular paper, "
#~ "inks, and even image characteristics (if you are printing a series of "
#~ "images with a color palette limited to subdued browns, you don't need a "
#~ "printer profile that tries to make room for saturated cyans and blues). I "
#~ "cannot offer any more advice or links to more information on this subject "
#~ "because I've just started to learn about printing images (previously I've "
#~ "only viewed and shared my images via monitor display). But do see <ulink "
#~ "url=\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/essays/fancy-graphics2.shtml"
#~ "\">this page</ulink> for an excellent presentation of the benefits of "
#~ "producing your own printer profile, plus a resoundingly positive "
#~ "endorsement of using Argyll for making your printer profile."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Whew!  Došli smo daleko - skoro smo spremni za printanje slike! Već znate "
#~ "odgovor na pitanje gdje dobiti profil printera. MOžete koristiti "
#~ "generički profil koji dolazi sa printerom. Možete kupiti profesionalno "
#~ "proizvedeni profil. Ako pitate, neke ustanovekomercijalno printanja će "
#~ "Vam poslati njihove profile (koje neće raditi sa vašim printerom). Možete "
#~ "napraviti sami profil koristeći Argyll, u tom slučaju će taj profil biti "
#~ "skrojen prema određenom papiru, tinti, čak i karakteristikama slike (ako "
#~ "printate seriju slika sa paletom boje ograničenom ublažene smeđe tonove, "
#~ "ne trebate profil koji pokušava naraviti prostor za  zasićene tirkizne i "
#~ "plave nijanse). Ne mogu ponuditi više savjeta ili linkova  sa više "
#~ "informacija o ovoj temi zato što  tek učim o printanju slika. Ali "
#~ "pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/essays/fancy-"
#~ "graphics2.shtml\">tovu stranicu</ulink> za odličnu prezentaciju o "
#~ "prednostima pravljenja vlastitog profila, plus glasno pozitivni odobrenje "
#~ "korištenja Argylla za pravljenje profila za printer."

#~ msgid "What about rendering intents?"
#~ msgstr "Šta je sa povratnim namjerama?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "\"Rendering intent\" refers to the way color gamuts are handled when the "
#~ "intended target color space (for example, the monitor or the printer) "
#~ "cannot handle the full gamut of the source color space (for example the "
#~ "working space)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "\"Povratna namjera\" se odnosi na način upravljanja skalama boja kada "
#~ "određena meta (npr, monitor ili printer)prostora booje ne može da podnese "
#~ "cijelu skalu izvornog prostora boja (npr. radni prostor)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are four commonly-used rendering intents: perceptual, relative "
#~ "colorimetric, absolute colorimetric, and saturation. I have searched the "
#~ "Internet looking for the best write-up on rendering intents and the trade-"
#~ "offs involved in choosing one rendering intent over another. I believe I "
#~ "found that article. See <ulink url=\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/"
#~ "tutorials/color-space-conversion.htm\">this page</ulink>. Briefly quoting "
#~ "from the Cambridge in Color article on color space conversion:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoje 4 često korištene povratne namjere :perceptivna, relativna "
#~ "kolorimetrija, apsolutna kolorimetrija, i zasićenje. Pretragom po "
#~ "internetu  tražili smo  najbolji materijal za povratne namjere i ramjene "
#~ "uključujući izabir jedne opcije između ostalih. Pogledajte <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/color-space-conversion.htm"
#~ "\">ovu stranicu </ulink>. Kratak citat sa CamBridge-ove stranice o "
#~ "konverizi profila boja:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Perceptual and relative colorimetric rendering are probably the most "
#~ "useful conversion types for digital photography. Each places a different "
#~ "priority on how they render colors within the gamut mismatch region."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Perceptivna i relativna kolorimetrijasu vjerovatno najkorisniji tipovi "
#~ "konverzije za digitalne fotografije. Svaka postavlja različit prioritet o "
#~ "tome kako vraćaju boje  kroz skalu promajašaja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Relative colorimetric maintains a near exact relationship between in "
#~ "gamut colors, even if this clips out of gamut colors."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Relativna kolorimetrija održava blistu konkretnu vezu između skale boja, "
#~ "čak i ako ovo siječe boje iz skale."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In contrast, perceptual rendering tries to also preserve some "
#~ "relationship between out of gamut colors, even if this results in "
#~ "inaccuracies for in gamut colors..."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Suprotno, perceptualno vraćanje pokušava čuvati neke veze između oja "
#~ "izvan skale, čak i ako ovo rezultuje  nepreciznostima za skalu."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Absolute is similar to relative colorimetric in that it preserves in "
#~ "gamut colors and clips those out of gamut, but they differ in how each "
#~ "handles the white point... Relative colorimetric skews the colors within "
#~ "gamut so that the white point of one space aligns with that of the other, "
#~ "while absolute colorimetric preserves colors exactly (without regard to "
#~ "changing white point). ..."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Apsolutna je slična relativnoj kolorimetriji u tome da čuva skalu i "
#~ "izbacuje one koje su izvan, ali se razlikuju po tome kako upravljaju "
#~ "bijelom tačkom. Relativna kolorimetrija iskrivljuje  boje unutar skale  "
#~ "tako da se bijela tačka jednog prostora poravnava sa onom iz drugog "
#~ "prostora, dok apsolutna kolorimetrija čuva tačne boje (bez mijenjenja "
#~ "bijele tačke)."

#~ msgid "Saturation rendering intent tries to preserve saturated colors."
#~ msgstr "Zasićenje pokušava održati zasićenost boja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "I would quote the entire article (it's that good), but that would involve "
#~ "\"unfair usage\" I am sure. So go check out the article for yourself. The "
#~ "illustrations in the article really help to clarify what the different "
#~ "rendering intents actually do and the compromises involved in choosing "
#~ "one rendering intent over another."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Citirali bismo cijeli članak (toliko je dobar), ali to bi uključili "
#~ "\"nepotrebne stvari\". Tako da provjerite sami članak. Ilustracije unutar "
#~ "članka pomoći će Vam da razjasnite  šta rade različite povraten namjere  "
#~ "i uključene kompromise u odabiru jednog."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For another excellent source of information on rendering intents with "
#~ "accompanying illustrations, see <ulink url=\"http://www.normankoren.com/"
#~ "color_management.html#Rendering_intent\">this page</ulink>."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Za drugi odličan izvor  sa pratećim ilustracijama, pogledjte <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://www.normankoren.com/color_management.html#Rendering_intent\">ovu "
#~ "stranicu</ulink>."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "What rendering intent should I use for displaying images on my monitor?"
#~ msgstr "Koju povratnu namjeru da koristim za prikaz slika na monitor?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The usual choice is relative colorimetric. I would suggest that you not "
#~ "use absolute colorimetric (&eg; with ufraw) unless you want very strange "
#~ "results."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Standardni izbor je relativna kolorietrija. Preporučujemo da ne koristite "
#~ "apsolutnu kolorimetriju (&eg; sa ufraw-om) osim ako ne žilite weoma čudne "
#~ "rezultate."

#~ msgid "What is soft-proofing?"
#~ msgstr "Šta je soft-proofing?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Soft-proofing will show you the differences to be expected between what "
#~ "you see on your screen and what you will see when you make a print. To "
#~ "soft-proof, you need a profile for your printer (actually, for your "
#~ "printer-paper combination, as the paper used affects the ink colors and "
#~ "the white point). If you don't like the soft-proofed image, you can make "
#~ "changes (in your working space, not after converting the image to your "
#~ "printer space!) to bring the soft-proofed image more in line with how you "
#~ "want the final print to look."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Soft-proofing će Vam pokazati kakve razlike d očekujete između onoga što "
#~ "vidite na ekranu i onoga što printate. Za soft-proof, rebate profil za "
#~ "printer (zapravo, za vašu kombinaciju printera-papira, kako korišteni "
#~ "papir utiče na boju tinte i bijelu tačku). Ako ne želite da primjenite "
#~ "soft-proof ne sliku, možete napraviti izmjene (u Vašm radnom prostoru, ne "
#~ "nakon konverzije slike u prostor printera!) da približite  soft-proof "
#~ "sliku onako kako želite da izgleda isprintana slika."

#~ msgid "What rendering intent should I use when I soft-proof?"
#~ msgstr "Koje povratne namjere trebam koristiti za primjenu  soft-proof-a?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "I've always heard that you ought to use \"perceptual intent\" when "
#~ "transforming an image from a larger working space to a smaller printer "
#~ "space. But especially in light of reading the aforementioned Cambridge in "
#~ "Color article, it seems that perceptual intent may or may not give the "
#~ "best results, depending on the respective gamuts of the image and printer/"
#~ "paper combination in question. I've been experimenting quite a bit lately "
#~ "with output intents for printing. I find that for my images, the "
#~ "colorimetric intents give clearer, brighter colors, albeit at the cost of "
#~ "having to carefully re-edit the image to avoid clipping highlights and "
#~ "shadows. Perusal of the various photography forums and articles available "
#~ "on the Internet indicates that \"perceptual intent\" is just an option, "
#~ "not by any means always \"the best\" option."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Često se čuje da bi treali koristiti \"perceptivnu namjeru \" kada se "
#~ "transformiše slika sa većeg radnog prostora u manji printerov prostor. "
#~ "Ali posebno zbog jednostavnosti čitanja ranije spomenutog CamBridge-ovog "
#~ "članka, čini se da perceprivna namjera može a i ne mora dati najbolje "
#~ "rezultate, u zavisnosti od datih cokbinacija skala slike i printera/"
#~ "papira. Eksperimentisali smo  sa izlaznim namjerama za printanje. Smatram "
#~ "da za moje slike, kolorimetrijske nmjere daju čišće, svjetlije boje, čak "
#~ "po cijenu preciznog preuređivanja  slike zbog izbjegavanja isjecanja "
#~ "naglasaka i sjena. Pregled različitih foruma fotografija  i člana "
#~ "dostupnih na internetu pokazuju da su \"povratne namjere\" samo opcije, "
#~ "ali ni u kojem slučaju najbolja opcija."

#~ msgid "And what about black point compensation?"
#~ msgstr "A šta je sa nadoknadom crne tačke ?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The clearest definition I could find about black point compensation is as "
#~ "follows: \"BPC is a way to make adjustments between the maximum black "
#~ "levels of digital files and the black capabilities of various digital "
#~ "devices [such as a printer]\" (cited from <ulink url=\"http://www."
#~ "newsandtech.com/issues/2004/05-04/pt/05-04_blackpoint.htm\">this page</"
#~ "ulink>)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Najjasnija definicija pronađena o nadoknadi crne tačke : \"\" BPC je "
#~ "način prilagođavanja između crnih nivoa digitalnih datoteka i crnih "
#~ "mogućnosti  različitih digitalnih uređaja [kao što je printer]\" (citat "
#~ "sa  <ulink url=\"http://www.newsandtech.com/issues/2004/05-04/"
#~ "pt/05-04_blackpoint.htm\">ove stranice</ulink>)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The article from which this definition comes offers a very clear "
#~ "explanation (albeit Adobe-centric) of how black point compensation works "
#~ "and the practical consequences of using or not using it. The bottom line "
#~ "advice is, it depends. Try soft-proofing with black point compensation "
#~ "on. If you like it, use it. Otherwise, don't use it."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Članak iz kojeg dolazi ova definicija nudi veoma jasna objašnjenja (iako "
#~ "Adobe-orjentisana)kako radi nadoknada crne tačke  i praktične posljedice "
#~ "korištenja i nekorištenja iste. Savjet je, zavisi. Probajte soft-proofing "
#~ "sa uključenom nadoknadom crne tačke . Ako Vam se sviđa koristite. U "
#~ "suprotnom, nemojte."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Can all of the rendering intents be used when converting from one color "
#~ "space to another?"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Mogu li se sve povratne namjere koristiti pri konverziji  iz jednog "
#~ "prostora u drugi?"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In a word, no. Which rendering intents are available when converting from "
#~ "one profile to another depends on the destination profile. Not every "
#~ "profile supports every rendering intent. What happens when you select an "
#~ "unsupported rendering intent is that LCMS quietly uses the profile's "
#~ "default rendering intent."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ne mogu. Koje su namjere dostupne pri konverziji iz jednog profila u "
#~ "drugi zavisi od odredišta profila. Ne podržava svaki profil povratne "
#~ "namjere. LCMS ćutke koristi zadani profil ako izaberete  nepodrđanu "
#~ "opciju ."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For an informative and humorous discussion of myths surrounding the use "
#~ "of various rendering intents, see <ulink url=\"http://www.colorwiki.com/"
#~ "wiki/Color_Management_Myths_21-25#Myth_.2321:"
#~ "_There_are_perceptual_rendering_intents_available_when_converting_from_scanner.2Fcamera-.3Eworkspace_or_workspace-.3Eworkspace."
#~ "\">here</ulink> and <ulink url=\"http://www.colorwiki.com/wiki/"
#~ "Color_Management_Myths_6-10\">here</ulink>."
