#~ msgid ""
#~ "The Universal Translator: your camera profile, the Profile Connection "
#~ "Space, and LMCS"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Univerzalni prevodioc: profil kamere, Profil povezivanja prostora, i LMCS"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are two commonly used Profile Connection Spaces - CIELAB and CIEXYZ "
#~ "(see <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_management\">Color "
#~ "management</ulink>, section on color translation, then look up CIELAB and "
#~ "CIEXYZ on wikipedia). Lcms uses the camera profile to translate the RGB "
#~ "values from the interpolated raw file, that is, the tiff produced by "
#~ "dcraw, into the appropriate Profile Connection Space (usually CIEXYZ - "
#~ "why CIEXYZ? I haven't taken the time to learn). A profile connection "
#~ "space is not itself a working space. Rather a PCS is an absolute "
#~ "reference space used only for translating from one color space to another "
#~ "- think of a PCS as a Universal Translator for all the color profiles "
#~ "that an image might encounter in the course of its journey from camera "
#~ "raw file to final output:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoje dva obično korištena Profila povezivanja prostora - CIELAB i "
#~ "CIEXYZ (pogledajte  <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
#~ "Color_management\">Upravljanje bojama</ulink>, dio o prevođenju boja, "
#~ "onda pogledajte CIELAB i CIEXYZ na  wikipediji). Lcm koristi profil "
#~ "kamere za prevođenje RGB vrijednosti  iz interpolirane raw datoteke, što "
#~ "značim tiff prozveden dcraw-om, u prikladan profil povezivanja prostora "
#~ "(obično CIEXYZ- zašto CIEXYZ nije bilo prilike da saznam tu informaciju). "
#~ "Profil povezivanja prostora sam nije radni prostor. Prije je CS apsolutni "
#~ "referencirani prostor koji se koristi samo za prevođenje iz jednog "
#~ "prostora boje u drugi - zamislite PCS kao univerzalnog prevodioca za sve "
#~ "profile boja koje slika može susteri naravno na ovom putvanju od raw "
#~ "datoteke  kamere do izlaza:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Lcms uses the camera profile, also called an input profile, to translate "
#~ "the interpolated dcraw-produced RGB numbers, which only have meaning "
#~ "relative to your (make and model of) camera, to a second set of RGB "
#~ "numbers that only have meaning in the Profile Connection Space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Lcms koristi profil kamere, također poznat kao ulazni profil, za "
#~ "prevođenje interpolirane RGB brojeve koje je proizveo dcraw, što ima "
#~ "značenje poznato samo kameri,  do drugog skupa RGB brojeva koje imaju "
#~ "značenje samo u profilu povezivanja prostora."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Lcms translates the Profile Connection Space RGB numbers to the "
#~ "corresponding numbers in your chosen working space so you can edit your "
#~ "image. And again, these working space numbers ONLY have meaning relative "
#~ "to a given working space. The same red, visually speaking, is represented "
#~ "by different trios of RGB numbers in different working spaces; and if you "
#~ "assign the wrong profile the image will look wrong, slightly wrong or "
#~ "very wrong depending on the differences between the two profiles."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Lcms prevodi RGB brojeve profila povezivanja prostora u odgovarajuće "
#~ "brojeve u odabranom radnom prostoru tako da možete uređivati sliku. "
#~ "Ponovo, ovi brjevi radnih prostora SAMO imaju značenje poznato datom "
#~ "radnom prostoru. Ista crvena, vizualno govoreći, predstavljena je "
#~ "različitim trijima RGB brojeva u različitim radnim prostorima; i ako "
#~ "dodijelite  pogrešan profil  slika će izgledati pogrešno, neznatno "
#~ "pogrešno ili skroz pogrešno zavisno od razlika ta dva profila."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "While you are editing your image in your chosen working space, then lcms "
#~ "should translate all the working space RGB numbers back to the PCS, and "
#~ "then over to the correct RGB numbers that enable your monitor (your "
#~ "display device) to give you the most accurate possible display "
#~ "representation of your image as it is being edited. This translation for "
#~ "display is done on the fly and you should never even notice it happening, "
#~ "unless it doesn't happen correctly - then the displayed image will look "
#~ "wrong, perhaps a little wrong, perhaps really, really, really wrong."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Dok uređujete slike u odabranom radnom prostoru, lcms bi trebao prevesti "
#~ "sve RGB brojeve nazad u PCS, i onda preko tačnih brojev koje omogućava "
#~ "Vaš monitor da Vam da najprecizniju moguću reprezentaciju slike koju ste "
#~ "uređivali. Prevođenje za ekran je gotovo u letu   nikada nebiste trebali "
#~ "primjetiti da se dešava, osim ako se ne dešava ispravno - onda će "
#~ "prikazana slika izgledati pogrešno, možda malo pogrešno, možda veoma, "
#~ "veomo pogrešno."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "When you are satisfied that your edited image is ready to share with the "
#~ "world, lcms translates the working space RGB numbers back into the PCS "
