#~ "ulink>"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Working spaces, such as sRGB or Adobe RGB, are color spaces that "
#~ "facilitate good results while editing. For instance, pixels with equal "
#~ "values of RGB should appear neutral. Using a large (gamut) working space "
#~ "will lead to posterization, while using a small working space will lead "
#~ "to clipping. This trade-off is a consideration for the critical image "
#~ "editor"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Radni prostori, kao što su sRGB ili Adobe RGB, su prostori boja koji "
#~ "olakšavaju dobre rezultate dok se uređuje.  Na primjer, pikseli sa istim "
#~ "vrijednostima RGB-a bi se trebali pojavljivati nautralni. Korištenje "
#~ "velikog (skala) radnog prostora će odvesti do posterizacije, dok "
#~ "korištenje manjih radnih prostora će dovesti do sjeckanja. Ova razmjena "
#~ "je prekretnica za kritični uređivač slika"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Well, that quote from wikipedia is about as clear as mud and I don't know "
#~ "if I will be able to explain it more clearly, but I will try. \"[P]ixels "
#~ "with equal values of RGB should appear neutral\" just means that for any "
#~ "given pixel in an image that has been converted to a suitable working "
#~ "space, if R=G=B you should see grey or black or white on your screen."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Dakle, taj citat sa wikipedije je mutan, i ne zna da li ću moći da ga "
#~ "objasnim jasnije, ali ću pokušati. \"[P]ikseli  sa jednakim vrijednostima "
#~ "RGB-a bi se trebali pojavljivati neutralni\" znači da za bilo koji piksel "
#~ "u slici koji je konvertovan u odgovarajući radni prostor, ako je R=G=B "
#~ "trebali biste vidjeti sivu, crnu, ili bijelu na vašem ekranu."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "I am not aware of a list of other technical requirements for a suitable "
#~ "working space, though undoubtedly someone has produced such a list. But "
#~ "most working space profiles are characterized by:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Nije poznata lista drugih tehničkih zahjeva za prikladan radni prostor, "
#~ "iako je nesumnjivo neko napravio takvu listu. Ali većina profila radnih "
#~ "prostora je okarakterisano:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "RGB primaries which dictate the range of colors, that is, the gamut "
#~ "covered by a given profile"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "RGB primarima koji diktiraju opseg boja, što znači, skala pokrivena datim "
#~ "profilom"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "white point, usually D50 or D65, which dictates the total dynamic range "
#~ "of the working space, from 0,0,0 (total black) to the brightest possible "
#~ "white"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "bijela tačka, obično  D50 ili D65, koja određuje ukupni dinamički opseg "
#~ "radnoog prostora, od 0,0,0 (totalna crna) do najsvjetlije moguće bijele"

#~ msgid "gamma"
#~ msgstr "gamma"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The practical consequences that result from using different RGB "
#~ "primaries, leading to larger or smaller working spaces, are discussed "
#~ "below. The practical consequences for different choices for the working "
#~ "space white point are beyond the scope of this tutorial. Here I will talk "
#~ "a little bit about the practical consequences of the working space gamma "
#~ "(for an excellent article and references, look up gamma on wikipedia)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Praktične posljedice koje nastaju upotrebom različitih RGB primara, "
#~ "vodeći do većih ili manjih radnih prostora, diskutovane su ispod. "
#~ "Praktične posljedice za različite izbore bijele tačke radnih prostora su "
#~ "ispod obima ovog tutorijala. Ovdje ćemo reći malo o praktičnim "
#~ "posljedicama gamme radnog prostora(za odličan članak i reference, "
#~ "pogledajte gammu na wikipediji)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The gamma of a color profile dictates what power transform needs to take "
#~ "place to properly convert from an image's embedded color profile (perhaps "
#~ "your working color space) to another color profile with a different "
#~ "gamma, such as (i)the display profile used to display the image on the "
#~ "screen or (ii)perhaps to a new working space, or (iii)perhaps from your "
#~ "working space to your printer's color space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Gamma profila boja određuje koja snaga transformacije je potrebna da se "
#~ "pravilno pretvori ili ugrađenog profila slike (možda Vašeg radnog "
#~ "prostora boje) u drugi profil sa drugom gammom, kao što su (i)profili "
#~ "ekrana koji se koriste za prikazivanje slike na ekranu ili (ii) možda za "
#~ "novi radni prostor, ili (iii) možda iz radnog prostora u printerov "
#~ "prostor boja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Mathematically speaking, for a power transform you normalize the RGB "
#~ "numbers and raise the resulting numbers to an appropriate power depending "
#~ "on the respective gammas of the starting and ending color space, then "
#~ "renormalize the results to a new set of RGB numbers. Lcms does this for "
#~ "you when you ask lcms to convert from one color space to another; "
#~ "however, if ALL you are doing is a power transform, use imagemagick "
#~ "instead of lcms and just manipulate the RGB numbers directly - the "
#~ "results will be more accurate."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Matematički govoreći, Za snagu transformacije normalizirate RGB brojeve  "
#~ "i podižete rezultujuće brojeve na prikladnu snagu u zavisnosti od "
#~ "određene gamme početnog i krajnjeg prostora, onda renormalizirate "
#~ "rezultate u novi skup RGB vrijednosti. Lcms ovo radi za Vas kada tražite "
#~ "lcms da prebaci iz jednog u drugi prostor; međutim, ako je SVE što Vi "
#~ "radite promjena snage, koristite imagemagick umjesto lcms.a i samo "
#~ "anipulišite RGB brojevima direktno - rezultat ća biti precizniji."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "One practical consequence of the gamma of a working space is that the "
#~ "higher the gamma, the more tones are available for editing in the "
#~ "shadows, with consequently fewer tones available in the highlights. So "
#~ "theoretically, if you are working on a very dark-toned (low key) image "
#~ "you might want a working space with a higher gamma. And if you are "
#~ "working on a high key image, say a picture taken in full noon sunlight of "
#~ "a wedding dress with snow as a backdrop, you might want to choose a "
#~ "working space with a lower gamma, so you have more available tonal "
#~ "gradations in the highlights. But in the real world of real image "
#~ "editing, almost everyone uses working spaces with either gamma 1.8 or 2.2."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Jedna praktična posljedica gamme radnog prostora je da što je veća gamma, "
#~ "više tonova je dosupno za uređivanje sjena,  samim tim manje tonova "
#~ "dostupno za naglašavanje. Teoretski, ako radite na jako tamnoj (niski "
#~ "ključ) slici trebate uzeti veću gammu. A ako radite sa visokim ključem, "
#~ "recimo slika vjenčanice uslikana u podne pod najjačim suncem sa snijegom "
#~ "u pozadini, onda trebate uzeti  radni prostor sa manjom gammom, tako da "
#~ "imate veći izbor tonova za naglašavanje prelaza. U stvarnom svijetu "
#~ "stvarnog uređivanja slika, skoro svi koriste radne prostore sa gammom 1.8 "
#~ "ili 2.2."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Some people are trying to standardize on gamma 2.0. sRGB and LStar-RGB "
#~ "are not gamma-based working spaces. Rather, sRGB uses a <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SRGB\">hybrid gamma</ulink>, and LStar-RGB "
#~ "uses a luminosity-based tonal response curve instead of a gamma value - "
#~ "see <ulink url=\"http://www.colormanagement.org/en/workingspaces.html"
#~ "\">here</ulink> for more information, and then google around for more in-"
#~ "depth information."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Neki ljudi pokušavaju standardizovati na gammu  2.0. sRGB i LStar-RGB "
#~ "nisu radni prostori zasnovani na gammi . Nego, sRGB koristi <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SRGB\">hibridnu gammu</ulink>, a LStar-RGB "
#~ "koristi tonalitetnu krivu zasnovanu na svjetlosti umjesto gamma "
#~ "vrjednosti - pogledjte <ulink url=\"http://www.colormanagement.org/en/"
#~ "workingspaces.html\">ovdje </ulink> za više informacija, i pretražite "
#~ "google za dublje informacije."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In addition to gamma 1.8 and gamma 2.2 the only other gamma for a working "
#~ "space that gets much mention or use is gamma 1.0, also called linear "
#~ "gamma. <emphasis>Linear gamma</emphasis> is used in HDR (high dynamic "
#~ "range) imaging and also if one wants to avoid introducing gamma-induced "
#~ "errors into one's regular low dynamic range editing. Gamma-induced errors "
#~ "is a topic outside the scope of this tutorial, but see <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://www.4p8.com/eric.brasseur/gamma.html\">Gamma errors</ulink> in "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.21stcenturyshoebox.com/essays/color_reproduction."
#~ "html\">picture scaling,</ulink> for gamma-induced color shifts."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "U dodatku gamme 1.8 i gamme 2.2 jedina druga gamma za radni prostor koja "
#~ "se mnogo spominje li koristi je gamma 1.0, također poznata kao i linearna "
#~ "gamma. <emphasis>Linearna gamma</emphasis> se koristi  u HDR-u (visokom "
#~ "dinamičkom opsegu) i također ako se želi izbjeći uvođenje gamma-"
#~ "indukovanih grešaka u regularnom niskom dinamičkom opsegu. Gamma-"
#~ "inducirane greške su tema izvan opsega ovog tutorijala, ali pogledajte "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.4p8.com/eric.brasseur/gamma.html\">Gamma greške</"
#~ "ulink> u dijelu <ulink url=\"http://www.21stcenturyshoebox.com/essays/"
#~ "color_reproduction.html\">skaluranje slika,</ulink> za gamma-inducirano "
#~ "pomijeranje boja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Unfortunately and despite their undeniable mathematical advantages, "
#~ "linear gamma working spaces have so few tones in the shadows that (in my "
#~ "opinion) they are impossible to use for editing if one is working in 8-"
#~ "bits, and still problematic at 16-bits. When the day comes when we are "
#~ "all doing our editing on 32-bit files produced by our HDR cameras on our "
#~ "personal supercomputers, I predict that we will all be using working "
#~ "spaces with gamma 1; Adobe Lightroom is already using a linear gamma "
#~ "working space \"under the hood\" and Lightzone has always used a linear "
#~ "gamma working space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Nažalost i uprkos njihovim nepobitnim matematičkim prednostima, linearne "
#~ "gamme radnih prostora imaju jako malo tonova u sjenama da su (po mom "
#~ "mišljenju) nemogući za korištenje za uređivanje ako se radi u 8-bitnom "
#~ "prostoru, a problematiččno je i za 16-bita. Kada dođe dan kada svi budemo "
#~ "uređivali 32-bitne datoteke koje su proizvele HDR kamere na našim super "
#~ "kompjuterima, predviđam da ćemo koristiti  radne prostore sa gammom 1; "
#~ "Adobe Lightroom već koristi radni prostor sa linearnom gammom \"ispod "
#~ "haube\" a Lightzone je uvijek koristio radni prostor sa linearnom gammom."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Which working space: <emphasis>large gamut</emphasis> or <emphasis>small "
#~ "gamut</emphasis>"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Koji radni prostor: <emphasis>velika skala</emphasis> ili <emphasis>mala "
#~ "skala</emphasis>"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "One MAJOR consideration in choosing a working space is that some working "
#~ "spaces are bigger than others, meaning they cover more of the visible "
#~ "spectrum (and perhaps even include some imaginary colors - mathematical "
#~ "constructs that don't really exist). These bigger spaces offer the "
#~ "advantage of allowing you to keep all the colors captured by your camera "
#~ "and preserved by the lcms conversion from your camera profile to the "
#~ "really big profile connection space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Jedna GLANA stvar koju treba razmotriti u odabiru radnog prostora je  da "
#~ "su neki prostori veći od drugih, što znači da pokrivaju veći dio "
#~ "vidljivog sprektra (i možda čak uključuju neke imaginarne boje - "
#~ "matematičke konstrukcije koje zaparavo ne postoje). Ovi veći prostori "
#~ "nude prednost koja Vam omogućava da zadržite  sve boje uhvaćene kamerom i "
#~ "očuvane lcms konverzijom iz profila kamere u jedan veliki prostor "
#~ "povezivanja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "But keeping all the possible colors comes at a price. It seems that any "
#~ "given digital image (pictures of daffodils with saturated yellows being "
#~ "one common exception) likely only contains a small subset of all the "
#~ "possible visible colors that your camera is capable of capturing. This "
#~ "small subset is easily contained in one of the smaller working spaces. "
#~ "Using a very large working space mean that editing your image (applying "
#~ "curves, saturation, etc) can easily produce colors that your eventual "
#~ "output device (printer, monitor) simply cannot display. So the conversion "
#~ "from your working space to your output device space (say your printer) "
#~ "will have to remap the out of gamut colors in your edited image, some of "
#~ "which might even be totally imaginary, to your printer color space with "
#~ "its much smaller gamut, leading to inaccurate colors at best and at worst "
#~ "to banding (posterization - gaps in what should be a smooth color "
#~ "transition, say, across an expanse of blue sky) and clipping (your "
#~ "carefully crafted muted transitions across delicate shades of red, for "
#~ "example, might get remapped to a solid block of dull red after conversion "
#~ "to your printer's color space)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Čuvanje svih mogućih boja dolazi sa cijenom. Čini se da bilo koja "
#~ "digitalna slika (slike narcisa sa zasićenom žutom  su jedan čest "
#~ "izuzetak) vjerovatno sadrži samo mali podskup svih mogućih vidljivih boja "
#~ "koje je kamera u mogućnosti snimiti.  Ovaj mali podskup  se lako sastoji "
#~ "u jednom od manjih radnih prostora. Korištenje veoma velikog radnog "
#~ "prostora znači da uređivanje slike (primjena krivih, zasićenja, itd) može "
#~ "lako proizvesti boju koju Vaš izlazni uređaj (printer ili monitor) "
#~ "jednostavno ne može prikazati. Tako da konverzija iz Vašeg radnog "
#~ "prostora u prostor izlaznog uređaja (recimo vašeg printera) moraće "
#~ "remapirati boje izvan skale sa slike, od kojih neke mogu biti totalno "
#~ "imaginarne za prostor printera sa veoma malom skalom, vodeći do "
#~ "nepreciznih boja u najboljem a u nagorem slučaju do savijanja "
#~ "(posterizacije - praznine u kojim bi trebali biti glatki prelazi boja, "
#~ "recimo, preko plavetnila neba) i sjećenja (vaš pažljivo napravljen prelaz "
#~ "preko delikatnih nijansi crvene, npr. možda se reapiraju od tamne crne do "
#~ "masne crvene nakon konverzije u prostor boje printera)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "In other words, large gamut working spaces, improperly handled, can lead "
#~ "to lost information on output. Small gamut working spaces can clip "
#~ "information on input. Like Wikipedia says, it's a trade-off. Here is some "
#~ "oft-repeated advice:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Drugim riječima, radin prostori sa velikom skalom, kojima se napravilno "
#~ "rukuje, mogu odvesti do gubitka informacija na izlazu. Mala skala može "
#~ "isjeći informacije  na ulazu. Kako wikipedija kaže, to je razmjena. Evo "
#~ "često ponavljanog savjeta."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For images intended for the web, use (one of the) sRGB (variants - there "
#~ "are several)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Za slika namijenjene za internet, koristite (jednu od) sRGB (varijanti- "
#~ "postoji nekoliko)."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For the most accuracy in your image editing (that is, making the most of "
#~ "your \"bits\" with the least risk of banding or clipping when you convert "
#~ "your image from your working space to an output space), use the smallest "
#~ "working space that includes all the colors in the scene that you "
#~ "photographed, plus a little extra room for those new colors you "
#~ "intentionally produce as you edit."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Za najpreciznije uređivanje (što znači, pravljenje većine bita sa manjim "
#~ "rizikom od savijanja ili osijecanja kada pretvarate sliku iz radnog u "
#~ "izlazni prostor), koristite najmanji radni prostor koji uključuje sve "
#~ "boje sa mjesta fotografisanja, plus malo dodatnog prostora za nove boje "
#~ "koje ćete napraviti dok budete uređivali."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If you are working in 8-bits rather than 16-bits, choose a smaller space "
#~ "rather than a larger space."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ako radite sa 8-bita redije nego sa16-bita, izaberite manji prostor "
#~ "radije nego veći."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For archival purposes, convert your raw file to a 16-bit tiff with a "
#~ "large gamut working space to avoid loosing color information. Then "
#~ "convert this archival tiff to your working space of choice (saving the "
#~ "converted working tiff under a new name, of course). See <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://simon.tindemans.eu/essays/scenereferredworkflow\">here</ulink> "
#~ "for more details."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Za svrhe arhiviranja, pretvorite raw datoteku u 16-bitni tiff sa velikom "
#~ "skalo da izbjegnete gubitak podataka o boji. Onda pretvorite ovaj "
#~ "arhivski tiff u radni prostor po izboru (sniite pretvoreni radni tiff pod "
#~ "drugim imenom). Pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://simon.tindemans.eu/essays/"
#~ "scenereferredworkflow\">ovdje</ulink> za više detalja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The WHYs of these bits of advice regarding which working space are beyond "
#~ "the scope of this tutorial. See Bruce Lindbloom's excellent website "
#~ "(<ulink url=\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/\">Info, Information about "
#~ "RGB Working Spaces</ulink>) for a visual comparison of the gamut (array "
#~ "of included colors) of the various working color spaces. See <ulink url="
#~ "\"http://www.luminous-landscape.com/tutorials/prophoto-rgb.shtml\">here</"
#~ "ulink> and <ulink url=\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/sRGB-"
#~ "AdobeRGB1998.htm\">here</ulink> for a pro and con presentation, "
#~ "respectively, of the merits of using large gamut working spaces. And "
#~ "while you are on the <ulink url=\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/"
#~ "tutorials/sRGB-AdobeRGB1998.htm\">cambridgeincolour.com</ulink> website, "
#~ "check out the tutorial on color management."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "WHY ovih savjeta s obrzirom na radni prostor su daleko izvan opsega ovog "
#~ "tutorijala. Pogledajte Bruce Lindbloom-ovu odličnu stranicu  (<ulink url="
#~ "\"http://www.brucelindbloom.com/\">Info, Informacije o RGB Radnim "
#~ "prostorima</ulink>)  za vizualno poređenje skale (niz uključenih boja) "
#~ "različitih radnih prostora boja. Pogledajte <ulink url=\"http://www."
#~ "luminous-landscape.com/tutorials/prophoto-rgb.shtml\">ovdje</ulink> i "
#~ "<ulink url=\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/sRGB-AdobeRGB1998."
#~ "htm\">ovdje</ulink> za prezentaciju za i protiv, respektivno, zasluga "
#~ "korištenja velike skale radnih prostora. I dok ste na stranici  <ulink "
#~ "url=\"http://www.cambridgeincolour.com/tutorials/sRGB-AdobeRGB1998.htm"
#~ "\">cambridgeincolour.com</ulink>, pogledajte tutorijal o upravljanju "
#~ "bojama."

#~ msgid "Soft Proofing"
#~ msgstr "Soft Proofing"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Soft Proofing is a way of previewing on the screen (monitor) the result "
#~ "to be expected from an output on another device, typically a printer. "
#~ "Soft proofing will show you the difference to be expected before you "
#~ "actually do it (and waste your costly ink). So you can improve your "
#~ "settings without wasting time and money."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Soft Proofing je način pregledanja rezultata ne ekranu (monitoru) koji se "
#~ "očekuje od izlaza drugog uređaja, obično printera. Soft proofing će Vam "
#~ "pokazati razliku koju očekujete prije nego što nešto uradite (i potrošite "
#~ "dragocjenu tintu). Tako možete unaprijediti postavke bez trošenja novca i "
#~ "vremena."

#~ msgid "Rendering intention"
#~ msgstr "Povratne namjere"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Rendering intent refers to the way gamuts are handled when the intended "
#~ "target color space cannot handle the full gamut."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Povratna namjera se odnosi na način na koji se upravlja skalama kad "
#~ "određena meta obojenog prostora ne može podnijeti punu skalu."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<emphasis>Perceptual</emphasis>, also called Image or Maintain Full "
#~ "Gamut. This is generally recommended for photographic images. The color "
#~ "gamut is expanded or compressed when moving between color spaces to "
#~ "maintain consistent overall appearance. Low saturation colors are changed "
#~ "very little. More saturated colors within the gamuts of both spaces may "
#~ "be altered to differentiate them from saturated colors outside the "
#~ "smaller gamut space. Perceptual rendering applies the same gamut "
#~ "compression to all images, even when the image contains no significant "
#~ "out-of-gamut colors."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<emphasis>Perceptivni</emphasis>,  također poznati i kao Slika ili "
#~ "Održavanje cijele skale. Ovo se generalno preporučuje za fotografske "
#~ "slike. Skala boja  je proširena ili sabijena kada se kreće među "
#~ "prostorima boja da se održi konzistentan ukupan izgled. Nisko zasićene "
#~ "boje su promijenjene veoma malo.  Više zasićene boje unutar skale  oba "
#~ "prostora  mogu se mijenjati da se razlikuju  od zasićenih boja izvan "
#~ "prostora manje skale. Perceptivno predstavljanje primjenjuje isto "
#~ "sabijanje skale na sve slike, čak i kad slika sadrži beznačajne boje "
#~ "izvan skale."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<emphasis>Relative Colorimetric</emphasis>, also called Proof or Preserve "
#~ "Identical Color and White Point. Reproduces in-gamut colors exactly and "
#~ "clips out-of-gamut colors to the nearest reproducible hue."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<emphasis>Relativena kolorimetrija</emphasis>, također poznata i kao "
#~ "Dokaz ili Čuvanje identične boje ili Bijela taačka. Proizvodi boje unutar "
#~ "skale precizno i odsijeca boje skale najbliže traženoj nijansi."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<emphasis>Absolute Colorimetric</emphasis>, also called Match or Preserve "
#~ "Identical Colors. Reproduces in-gamut colors exactly and clips out-of-"
#~ "gamut colors to the nearest reproducible hue, sacrificing saturation and "
#~ "possibly lightness. On tinted papers, whites may be darkened to keep the "
#~ "hue identical to the original. For example, cyan may be added to the "
#~ "white of a cream-colored paper, effectively darkening the image. Rarely "
#~ "of interest to photographers."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<emphasis>Apsolutna Kolorimetrija</emphasis>,  također poznata kao "
#~ "Poklapanje ili Čuvanje identičnih boja. Reproducira boje unutar skale  "
#~ "tačno i siječe boje izvan skale na najblizi reprodukovanu nijansu, "
#~ "žrtvujući zasićenje i moguču svjetlinu. Na nijansiranim papirima,   "
#~ "bijele mogu biti potamnjene da se zadrži nijansaidentična originalnu. Na "
#~ "primjer, tirkizna se može dodati na bijeli ili bež papir, efektivno "
#~ "potamnjujući sliku. Rijetko u interesu fotografa."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<emphasis>Saturation</emphasis>, also called Graphic or Preserve "
#~ "Saturation. Maps the saturated primary colors in the source to saturated "
#~ "primary colors in the destination, neglecting differences in hue, "
#~ "saturation, or lightness. For block graphics; rarely of interest to "
#~ "photographers."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<emphasis>Zasićenje</emphasis>, također poznato kao Grafika ili Čuvanje "
#~ "zasićenja. Mapira zasićene primarne boje u izvoru do zasićenih primarnih "
#~ "boja na odredištu, zanemarujući  razlike u nijansi, zasićenju ili "
#~ "svjetlini. Za blokove grafike; rijetko interes fotografa."

